WEBVTT

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:22.270
"Kurokawa Mansion"

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:26.940
As Mr. Kurokawa sat at his word processor, having a drink,

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:29.820
"Kurokawa Daizo (62) -

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:29.820
Kurokawa Hospital Director"

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:30.230
Someone hit and killed him from behind.

00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:34.610
The weapon was undoubtedly the bronze statue lying next to him.

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:37.320
But this is what I don't understand.

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:42.160
While it appears to be a dying message, what does "JUN" mean?

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:46.630
It identifies the culprit, loud and clear.

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:48.000
Say what?!

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:51.300
What's more, the killer is one of those three!

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:54.050
<i>He's on the ball for once!</i>

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:56.800
"Kurokawa Mina (32) -

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:56.800
Daizo's Second Wife"

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:57.010
His wife, Kurokawa Mina-<i>san,</i>

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:59.760
"Kurokawa Daisuke (36) -

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:59.760
Eldest Son - Physician"

00:00:57.010 --> 00:00:59.760
his oldest son, Kurokawa Daisuke-<i>san,</i>

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:03.640
"Nakazawa Manami (27) - Housekeeper"

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:03.930
and his housekeeper, Nakazawa Manami-<i>san.</i>
One of these is the killer.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:07.650
Great, Mori-<i>kun</i>!
So, who is it?!

00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:10.610
The person who killed Kurokawa Taizo is...

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:12.030
...you!

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:14.070
H-his wife?!

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:18.660
The letters "JUN" that
Mr. Kurokawa left behind

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:23.200
correspond to the English word for the six month of the year: June.

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:27.460
This month can also be called <i>"Minazuki</i>" in Japanese.

00:01:27.630 --> 00:01:31.000
In other words, "Mina-<i>san".</i>
What's more, you...

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:35.300
So what if I was born in June?!
So what if "Mina" is in "<i>Minazuki</i>"?!

00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:38.390
You're gonna pin this on me with some lousy pun?!

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:42.220
No, no, this is a logical deduction based on...

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:46.640
Would someone on the verge of death do something so roundabout?

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:49.770
If it was me, I'd just type the killer's name straight out.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:51.650
Not you, too, Inspector?

00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:55.820
<i>That's the extent</i> <i>of his logic? Oh well...</i>

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:59.320
Is making innocent people out to be guilty what detectives do?!

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:02.200
<i>I'll do it like always and use</i> <i>this Anesthetic Watch Gun ...</i>

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:04.620
<i>to have the old man sleep again!</i>

00:02:06.910 --> 00:02:08.500
Here it comes!

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:10.670
Really?! I've been waiting!

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:18.340
Yes. I was merely joking when I said you were the killer.

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:19.890
Joking?

00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:22.680
Inspector Megure.
Take a close look at the body.

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:28.850
Mr. Kurokawa's right pinky is the only finger with blood on it.

00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:30.650
Indeed it is.

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:34.650
So, which parts of the keyboard have blood on them?

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:39.450
<i>"Ke", "mu", "ro</i>", and the uppercase
English key on the left side.

00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:44.290
The blood on the "<i>ke", "mu",</i> and "<i>ro</i>" keys came from his pinky

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:49.790
when Mr. Kurokawa typed "JUN" with his index finger,

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:55.800
but no one presses keys on the very left side with their right pinky.

00:02:57.090 --> 00:03:00.800
Then where did the blood on that left key come from?

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:06.720
Most likely, Mr. Kurokawa was hit from behind by the stealthy culprit,

00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:08.770
upon which he put his right hand to his head.

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:11.560
This is probably where the blood on his pinky came from.

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:14.520
Then, when he looked back, he was hit again,

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:18.190
and he knocked over the keyboard with his pinky as he fell.

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:23.370
In other words, the English uppercase key on the very left

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:26.910
was not pressed of Mr. Kurokawa's will at the time of the crime,

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:30.160
but just happened to be pressed as he fell instead.

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:37.670
Then, after the killer left,
Mr. Kurokawa used the last of his strength

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:39.800
to press the keys in front of him...

00:03:42.260 --> 00:03:44.350
...thinking he was typing in Japanese <i>kana.</i>

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:48.520
Then what would "JUN" have been in <i>kana</i>?!

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:51.480
"Manami"!

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:55.520
Yes. The housewife,
Nakazawa Manami-<i>san...</i>

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:57.070
You did it!

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:02.700
Y-you're joking, right, Detective?
There's no proof, after all...

00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:04.660
Oh, but there is proof.

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:09.450
You removed your slippers at the time of the crime, did you not?

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:14.580
Because the slippers would have made noise on the wood flooring,

00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:19.260
making it impossible for you to sneak up on Mr. Kurokawa unnoticed.

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:21.720
Unbeknownst to you...

00:04:24.050 --> 00:04:27.220
...you actually stepped in some of the blood on the ground.

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:33.140
The inexplicably missing bit of blood in Exhibit A proves this.

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:38.020
There should be blood on the bottom of your white sock!

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:49.540
You also said in your statement that you hadn't gotten near the body.

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:54.080
May I ask that we be allowed to examine the blood on your foot?

00:04:55.290 --> 00:05:00.300
Kurokawa killed my husband one year ago.

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:05.840
You mean the patient my old man did heart surgery on?!

00:05:05.930 --> 00:05:07.010
That's right!

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:10.970
I'm the wife of the patient who died after he operated on him drunk!

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:15.480
The fact no one noticed the simple changes to my hair and name

00:05:15.770 --> 00:05:21.110
means the incident wasn't big enough for any of you to remember it.

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:27.030
I tried to get testimonies from the hospital staff so I could accuse him,

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:29.700
but not a single person would help me!

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:32.370
They were all afraid of Kurokawa!

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:37.000
So you decided to avenge your husband...

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:39.710
Today was the anniversary of his death...

00:05:40.750 --> 00:05:42.710
I regret nothing!

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:45.300
I managed to get revenge for him!

00:05:58.440 --> 00:05:59.810
Let's go.

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:10.490
<i>Wound up giving him</i> <i>all the credit again...</i>

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:18.830
"Detective Conan -
The Time Bombed Skyscraper"

00:06:23.050 --> 00:06:25.840
<i>I'm high school detective Kudo Shinichi.</i>

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:30.510
Original Creator: Gosho Aoyama

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:30.510
(Serialized in Shogakukan's "Shonen Sunday")

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:30.510
Screenplay: Kazunari Kouchi

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:30.890
<i>I went with old friend and classmate,</i>
<i>Mori Ran, to an amusement park</i>

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:34.760
<i>where I witnessed a suspicious deal</i> <i>with a man dressed in black.</i>

00:06:34.140 --> 00:06:38.060
Music: Katsuo Ono

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:38.520
<i>I was so absorbed with watching the deal</i>

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:41.860
<i>that I didn't notice a second man</i> <i>sneak up from behind me!</i>

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:47.030
Character Design: Masatomo Sudô

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:47.030
Art Director: Yukihiro Shibutani

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:47.030
Director of Photography: Takashi Nomura

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:47.030
Sound Director: Katsuyoshi Kobayashi

00:06:43.730 --> 00:06:47.690
<i>He forced me to take a poison,</i> <i>and when I woke up...</i>

00:06:47.950 --> 00:06:50.240
<i>...my body had shrunk!</i>

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:54.700
<i>If they learned Kudo Shinichi was alive,</i> <i>they might go after me again,</i>

00:06:54.700 --> 00:06:56.870
<i>putting all the people</i> <i>around me in danger!</i>

00:06:57.120 --> 00:07:00.920
Conan Edogawa: Minami Takayama

00:06:57.290 --> 00:07:00.920
<i>Per Dr. Agasa's advice,</i>
<i>I decided to conceal my identity.</i>

00:07:01.040 --> 00:07:04.840
<i>When Ran asked my name,</i>
<i>I quickly answered, "Edogawa Conan."</i>

00:07:05.210 --> 00:07:06.960
<i>To get information on the men,</i>

00:07:07.050 --> 00:07:10.010
<i>I wound up living with Ran</i> <i>and her detective father.</i>

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:14.350
Ran Mori: Wakana Yamazaki

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:14.350
Kogoro Mori: Akira Kamiya

00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:14.010
<i>But the old guy's such</i> <i>a bonehead detective...</i>

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:16.640
<i>Unable to stand by and watch,</i>
<i>I took his place</i>

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:20.480
<i>and used my powers of deduction</i> <i>to solve tough case after tough case.</i>

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:21.770
Inspector Megure: Chafurin

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:21.770
Dr. Agasa: Kenichi Ogata

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:21.770
Shinichi Kudo: Kappei Yamaguchi

00:07:21.850 --> 00:07:25.690
<i>As a result, the old mars now</i> <i>a prominent and famous detective,</i>

00:07:21.850 --> 00:07:25.690
"Famous Detective Kogoro Mori"

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:29.490
<i>while I'm stuck doing</i> <i>grade school all over again.</i>

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:29.240
"Conan Edogawa"

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:32.570
<i>I even wound up in a</i> <i>"Junior Detective League"</i>

00:07:32.570 --> 00:07:35.450
<i>with my classmates Ayumi,</i>
<i>Genta, and Mitsuhiko.</i>

00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:35.950
"Junior Detective League"

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:42.580
Now let me introduce the gadgets the doctor has built for me!

00:07:42.710 --> 00:07:44.750
First is the Anesthetic Watch Gun!

00:07:45.090 --> 00:07:47.840
Pressing the button while using the aiming device on the cover

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:51.630
will launch an anesthetic needle that can knock a person out instantly.

00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:55.140
Next is the Voice-Altering Bow Tie!

00:07:55.260 --> 00:07:57.560
By adjusting the dials on the back,

00:07:57.560 --> 00:08:00.980
I can produce all types of voices, from children to adult!

00:08:01.230 --> 00:08:04.190
For offensive items,
I have the Power Kick Shoes!

00:08:04.270 --> 00:08:06.400
They use electricity and magnetic fields

00:08:06.570 --> 00:08:08.900
to stimulate my feet muscles and maximize my kick power!

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:12.910
To chase down criminals,
I have the Turbo-Engine Skateboard!

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:20.410
But as it's solar-powered, it can only be used when the sun is out.

00:08:15.410 --> 00:08:19.580
Producer: Masahito Yoshioka

00:08:15.410 --> 00:08:19.580
Michihiko Suwa

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:24.460
Director: Kenji Kodama

00:08:20.910 --> 00:08:22.580
Whoops, can't forget this one!

00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:26.460
The Junior Detective League's badges contain miniature transceivers

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:30.010
Speaker

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:30.010
Antenna

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:30.010
MIC

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:29.420
as well as transmitters!

00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:32.420
There are plenty of others,

00:08:33.010 --> 00:08:36.050
but my main weapon is undoubtedly this!

00:08:36.390 --> 00:08:40.100
Even when I'm small, my mind remains that of a sharp detective!

00:08:40.180 --> 00:08:42.100
There is always only one truth!

00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:45.730
"Dr. Agasa's House -

00:08:42.810 --> 00:08:45.730
April 26th (Saturday)"

00:08:45.730 --> 00:08:49.190
"To Kudo Yusaku..." "To Mr. Yusaku Kudo..."

00:08:45.730 --> 00:08:49.190
Air Express - Tomato Express Delivery

00:08:49.190 --> 00:08:53.110
"Edogawa Conan (Kudo Shinichi)"

00:08:49.570 --> 00:08:51.650
They're all to Dad...

00:08:51.820 --> 00:08:54.860
Probably all fan letters anyway...

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:59.790
Come to think of it, I hear your father's latest Night Baron book

00:08:59.990 --> 00:09:02.750
was a huge best seller in America, too!

00:09:02.830 --> 00:09:05.710
Yeah. But he's in Switzerland now.

00:09:05.710 --> 00:09:08.210
It's gotta be a pain sending him fan letters

00:09:08.290 --> 00:09:11.840
when he's constantly traveling all over the world.

00:09:11.960 --> 00:09:15.760
Well, the important thing is that he's getting to do what he wants.

00:09:15.760 --> 00:09:17.180
Yeah, yeah.

00:09:17.260 --> 00:09:19.970
Incidentally Doc, what're you making?

00:09:20.140 --> 00:09:21.720
A new gadget for me?

00:09:21.850 --> 00:09:24.690
Sorry, but it's nothing that paltry.

00:09:24.940 --> 00:09:29.270
Humankind studied the birds in the sky to create airplanes!

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:34.950
But no one has yet duplicated the wing-flapping mechanism of insects!

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:39.620
If I can create the very first one and sell it as a toy,

00:09:39.700 --> 00:09:43.700
I'll capture the interest of children the world over!

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:48.330
And then I'll get oodles of money and become a billionaire!

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:54.050
<i>And just when is that gonna be reality?</i>

00:09:54.050 --> 00:09:57.050
<i>I've been hearing him say that since I was a kid...</i>

00:09:57.880 --> 00:10:01.970
Still, the fact I never get fan letters anymore must mean

00:10:01.970 --> 00:10:04.430
that society has completely forgotten...

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:06.350
"To Kudo Shinichi"

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:06.940
It's to me.

00:10:06.600 --> 00:10:09.020
"Moriya Teiji"?

00:10:10.650 --> 00:10:12.400
<i>The</i> Moriya Teiji?

00:10:13.030 --> 00:10:16.530
"Please forgive the suddenness of my letter."

00:10:16.650 --> 00:10:19.570
"I've heard much about your exploits as a high school detective

00:10:19.570 --> 00:10:23.240
in the newspapers and on television,

00:10:23.330 --> 00:10:28.420
and very much wanted the chance to speak with you in person."

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:32.290
"Agasa Hiroshi (52) - Inventor"

00:10:28.710 --> 00:10:32.670
"As such, I would like to invite you to the afternoon tea garden party

00:10:32.880 --> 00:10:39.680
I am holding at my home on
Tuesday, April 29, at 3:30 pm."

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:42.300
"I do hope that you will attend."

00:10:43.760 --> 00:10:46.350
Oh, so it's a party invitation?

00:10:46.430 --> 00:10:49.230
Doc. You know who
Moriya Teiji is, right?

00:10:49.310 --> 00:10:51.060
I most certainly do!

00:10:51.060 --> 00:10:53.270
He's an architecture professor at Touto University.

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:55.860
And one of the best architects in all of Japan!

00:10:55.940 --> 00:10:58.740
Why would such a big shot want to invite me?

00:10:59.660 --> 00:11:05.540
Architecture is art, so he's probably always looking for inspiration.

00:11:05.620 --> 00:11:09.790
Plus, Professor Moriya is a master genius just like me!

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:16.920
<i>Master genius, indeed...</i>

00:11:18.510 --> 00:11:19.840
A garden party?

00:11:19.670 --> 00:11:27.100
"Mori Ran - Teitan High School Junior"

00:11:19.930 --> 00:11:24.850
Yeah. I can't make it, seeing as
I'm in the middle of this one case...

00:11:24.890 --> 00:11:27.220
So you want me to go in your place?

00:11:27.350 --> 00:11:30.270
The invitation said companions are welcome too,

00:11:30.350 --> 00:11:33.060
so you should go with your dad and that one kid living with you...

00:11:33.150 --> 00:11:34.270
What's his name again?

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:35.520
Conan-<i>kun</i>?

00:11:35.520 --> 00:11:41.030
Yeah. You three should go.
The invitation's in your mailbox now.

00:11:41.150 --> 00:11:45.330
Urgh! You hardly ever call, and when you do, it's for selfish reasons!

00:11:45.450 --> 00:11:47.620
Okay! But on one condition!

00:11:47.620 --> 00:11:48.700
Condition?

00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:52.330
See an all-night movie with me next Saturday!

00:11:52.330 --> 00:11:53.460
Eh?!

00:11:53.540 --> 00:11:56.170
Come on! I haven't seen you in a while!

00:11:56.170 --> 00:11:59.130
Meet me in the lobby of the Beika Cinema at 10:00 pm!

00:11:59.210 --> 00:12:03.590
W-wait! Next Saturday's no good!
Maybe later on when...

00:12:03.590 --> 00:12:06.760
No! We have to go during May 3rd!

00:12:07.680 --> 00:12:10.810
Say, which do you like better, red or blue?

00:12:10.890 --> 00:12:13.480
Red or blue?
What brought that on?

00:12:13.810 --> 00:12:15.650
Just answer!

00:12:15.810 --> 00:12:18.230
Well, red, I guess?

00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:23.450
Red? I should've guessed!
That's what I was going to say, too!

00:12:23.660 --> 00:12:26.490
<i>Well, red is your favorite color...</i>

00:12:26.490 --> 00:12:30.080
"Mori Kogoro - Private Detective"

00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:29.040
Hey, where's dinner?

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:31.120
Yes, yes, I'll get right on it.

00:12:31.410 --> 00:12:34.750
Alright, Shinichi! The night of the 3rd, at 10:00! Don't forget now!

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:37.040
Wait!

00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:38.340
Geez.

00:12:38.420 --> 00:12:42.970
If I could see a movie, I wouldn't have said I couldn't make a party.

00:12:45.050 --> 00:12:49.060
<i>Still, why does it have to be May 3rd?</i>

00:12:49.180 --> 00:12:51.430
<i>Did something happen on that day?</i>

00:12:51.640 --> 00:12:57.110
<i>May 4th is when Holmes and Moriarty</i> <i>fell into the Reichenbach Falls,</i>

00:12:57.860 --> 00:13:00.730
<i>and May 5th is Children's Day...</i>

00:13:00.730 --> 00:13:02.490
Hey, Conan-<i>kun</i>!

00:13:02.570 --> 00:13:04.150
On your way home?

00:13:04.150 --> 00:13:06.200
Inspector! On another case?!

00:13:05.950 --> 00:13:09.740
"Inspector Megure - Police HQ -

00:13:05.950 --> 00:13:09.740
Investigation 1st Division"

00:13:06.280 --> 00:13:07.910
Yes, on a couple...

00:13:08.030 --> 00:13:09.870
Oh, let me introduce you.

00:13:10.040 --> 00:13:13.410
This is my newest assistant, Shiratori-<i>kun.</i>

00:13:13.410 --> 00:13:17.420
My name's Shiratori.
The inspector's told me about you.

00:13:13.540 --> 00:13:17.250
"Inspector Shiratori

00:13:13.540 --> 00:13:17.250
Investigation 1st Division"

00:13:17.580 --> 00:13:20.210
I hear you notice interesting things...

00:13:20.380 --> 00:13:23.550
No, it's all just coincidence!

00:13:24.050 --> 00:13:28.180
Yes. Multiple coincidences are common...

00:13:28.430 --> 00:13:30.260
<i>Well, I'll be!</i>

00:13:30.260 --> 00:13:34.180
With all these incidents,
I won't get to relax during Golden Week.

00:13:34.310 --> 00:13:35.390
Bye!

00:13:37.900 --> 00:13:39.270
Golden Week?

00:13:39.770 --> 00:13:41.020
Oh, yeah!

00:13:42.820 --> 00:13:45.490
May 3rd is Constitution Memorial Day!

00:13:46.280 --> 00:13:48.030
And that's gotta do with what?

00:13:48.700 --> 00:13:50.030
Birthday?

00:13:50.410 --> 00:13:54.000
That's right!
May 4th is Shinichi's birthday!

00:13:54.250 --> 00:13:56.920
My plan is to invite him to an all-night movie on May 3rd,

00:13:57.170 --> 00:14:01.090
and then surprise him by handing him a red polo shirt for a present

00:14:01.340 --> 00:14:03.340
when the clock strikes midnight!

00:14:03.550 --> 00:14:06.680
<i>Oh, yeah!</i>
<i>May 4th is my birthday!</i>

00:14:06.800 --> 00:14:08.510
<i>I totally forgot...</i>

00:14:08.510 --> 00:14:11.140
So what movie are you seein'?

00:14:11.350 --> 00:14:12.930
"Legend of the Red Thread".

00:14:12.930 --> 00:14:14.430
Red thread?

00:14:14.520 --> 00:14:16.140
Oh, you never heard of it?

00:14:16.230 --> 00:14:19.440
It's a romantic movie based on a story about a man and a woman

00:14:19.440 --> 00:14:25.690
whose pinkies were connected by a red thread of destiny since birth!

00:14:25.690 --> 00:14:27.740
<i>Ick! That's so girly...</i>

00:14:27.900 --> 00:14:32.740
And look! Both Shinichi and I have red as our lucky color for May!

00:14:32.830 --> 00:14:35.540
So I decided that we gotta see this!

00:14:32.830 --> 00:14:35.290
Taurus

00:14:32.830 --> 00:14:35.290
KEY No.5 * RED * DEPART

00:14:35.620 --> 00:14:40.000
<i>That's nice, but there's</i> <i>no way I can see it with you...</i>

00:14:41.380 --> 00:14:45.670
Hold on! Didn't you say this was an all-night movie?!

00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:46.760
That's right...

00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:49.180
Forget it! I forbid it!

00:14:49.260 --> 00:14:53.760
A young man and woman getting all cozy in the dark, late at night...

00:14:53.760 --> 00:14:57.230
It's not like that!
Don't be creepy!

00:14:57.310 --> 00:15:01.100
Shinichi always forgets his birthday!

00:15:01.310 --> 00:15:04.230
I have to remind him every year!

00:15:04.320 --> 00:15:06.780
Otherwise he'd just get older and older!

00:15:08.070 --> 00:15:10.070
<i>Though I'm actually smaller now...</i>

00:15:10.070 --> 00:15:15.030
Yeah, but... He's still in high school...

00:15:14.120 --> 00:15:15.040
<i>Oh, yeah!</i>

00:15:15.540 --> 00:15:19.040
Dad! Let's go to Moriya Teiji's garden party!

00:15:19.210 --> 00:15:21.250
W-what brought that on?

00:15:21.500 --> 00:15:25.420
Shinichi was actually the one invited, but he can't make it...

00:15:25.710 --> 00:15:28.590
- Wanna come too, Conan-<i>kun</i>?

00:15:27.380 --> 00:15:28.590
- Yeah! I do!

00:15:29.510 --> 00:15:33.010
Like we can really go, using an invitation for Shinichi!

00:15:33.180 --> 00:15:36.470
Moriya Teiji is a famous architect, right?

00:15:36.560 --> 00:15:40.310
It'd be a historical meeting between great detective and great architect!

00:15:41.940 --> 00:15:44.110
Great detective and great architect, huh?!

00:15:46.520 --> 00:15:49.150
<i>He is so easy to manipulate...</i>

00:15:50.320 --> 00:15:54.070
"Moriya Mansion - April 29th (Tuesday)"

00:15:56.280 --> 00:15:59.290
Conan-<i>kun</i>! Wait!
We need the invitation!

00:16:05.250 --> 00:16:06.800
- Enjoy yourselves!
- Thanks!

00:16:12.430 --> 00:16:14.090
Wow!

00:16:14.300 --> 00:16:19.520
Truly a building from 17th century
England's House of Stewart era!

00:16:21.350 --> 00:16:23.600
You know a lot about architecture, Dad!

00:16:23.690 --> 00:16:27.270
Yes, I was once known as the Walking Library!

00:16:27.360 --> 00:16:29.780
More importantly, look closely at the left and right sides.

00:16:35.700 --> 00:16:36.620
Hey, look!

00:16:36.700 --> 00:16:40.160
When you stand in the middle, the left and right sides look the same!

00:16:40.450 --> 00:16:42.580
The garden and the building!

00:16:42.660 --> 00:16:46.790
This is what they call "symmetry"!

00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:50.710
Professor Moriya lived in England until high school,

00:16:50.800 --> 00:16:55.140
so he is quite fond of English-style architecture. In particular...

00:16:55.220 --> 00:16:57.300
In particular, uhh...

00:16:58.260 --> 00:17:03.310
His keenness for classical-style symmetry is remarkable!

00:17:02.020 --> 00:17:04.640
<i>A cheat sheet...</i>

00:17:04.640 --> 00:17:10.020
"Moriya Teiji"

00:17:04.980 --> 00:17:10.320
He even changed how he writes "Teiji" to give his name symmetry!

00:17:10.480 --> 00:17:12.280
<i>Almost sounds like a disease...</i>

00:17:12.740 --> 00:17:15.990
This is the first time I've seen such a wonderful garden!

00:17:16.070 --> 00:17:18.530
I thank you for your kind praise!

00:17:16.860 --> 00:17:20.660
"Moriya Teiji (47) - Architect"

00:17:18.740 --> 00:17:20.660
Hello, I am Moriya Teiji.

00:17:20.740 --> 00:17:25.120
I-I'm Mori Ran! This is my father, and Edogawa Conan-<i>kun.</i>

00:17:25.120 --> 00:17:29.000
Shinichi - I mean, Kudo-<i>kun</i> couldn't make it today,

00:17:29.000 --> 00:17:30.750
so we came in his place!

00:17:32.260 --> 00:17:35.590
I see. So Kudo-<i>kun</i> couldn't come...

00:17:35.760 --> 00:17:38.600
But this man's a famous detective, too!

00:17:39.390 --> 00:17:42.100
Hey! Whadya mean, "too"?!

00:17:45.810 --> 00:17:47.400
I'm Mori Kogoro.

00:17:47.480 --> 00:17:51.400
Oh! You're that famous detective!
Pleasure to meet you!

00:17:54.280 --> 00:17:57.660
Right this way.
The party is in the rear garden.

00:17:59.070 --> 00:18:01.080
The rear garden is just as wonderful!

00:18:01.950 --> 00:18:04.790
<i>Just what I'd expect</i> <i>from a famous architect's party...</i>

00:18:04.870 --> 00:18:10.420
<i>musicians, models, corporate execs,</i> <i>critics, and celebrities...</i>

00:18:10.540 --> 00:18:13.050
<i>All famous people from TV...</i>

00:18:14.050 --> 00:18:17.680
Please, make yourselves at home this afternoon!

00:18:19.260 --> 00:18:22.720
How pretty! Are these all homemade?

00:18:22.810 --> 00:18:27.810
But of course. It's only proper to serve homemade food at a tea party.

00:18:28.100 --> 00:18:29.770
Please, have some.

00:18:29.850 --> 00:18:31.060
Thank you!

00:18:32.770 --> 00:18:35.190
How does it taste?

00:18:35.190 --> 00:18:37.110
These cookies are delicious!

00:18:37.200 --> 00:18:39.320
I'm glad to hear it!

00:18:39.410 --> 00:18:42.620
Spending all night making them was worth it!

00:18:42.700 --> 00:18:45.540
Oh, Professor!
You cook?!

00:18:46.250 --> 00:18:48.670
I might not look it, but I am single.

00:18:48.670 --> 00:18:54.630
All the food here, the scones, sandwiches, cookies, I made it all.

00:18:54.710 --> 00:18:58.090
I'm the type who isn't satisfied unless I do everything myself...

00:18:58.260 --> 00:19:03.510
I see! That's the mentality that produces all those beautiful buildings?

00:19:03.680 --> 00:19:07.390
I do not consider something architecture if it is not beautiful!

00:19:07.890 --> 00:19:11.600
Most young architects these days lack artistic sense!

00:19:11.690 --> 00:19:15.690
They need to feel much more responsibility for their works!

00:19:17.820 --> 00:19:22.070
Incidentally, Mori-<i>san.</i>
Would you mind if I posed a quiz?

00:19:22.200 --> 00:19:23.950
A quiz?

00:19:23.950 --> 00:19:27.370
Yes. The goal is to deduce the password to a computer

00:19:27.370 --> 00:19:30.080
that three men use for their business,

00:19:30.420 --> 00:19:35.380
though I'm sure it will take the great
Mori Kogoro-<i>san</i> no time at all.

00:19:35.920 --> 00:19:38.300
He's the famous Mori Kogoro-<i>san</i>!

00:19:38.670 --> 00:19:39.880
Certainly!

00:19:40.340 --> 00:19:41.340
Go ahead!

00:19:41.340 --> 00:19:43.010
<i>Hey, now. You gonna be alright?</i>

00:19:43.260 --> 00:19:46.560
Well, then, here is the data on those three people.

00:19:46.720 --> 00:19:51.060
The password is a five-character word based on their commonalities.

00:19:51.560 --> 00:19:53.060
Would you like to try too, Ran-<i>san</i>?

00:19:55.060 --> 00:19:59.860
You have three minutes to solve it.
Please think it over, everyone.

00:20:05.780 --> 00:20:08.080
Ready, begin!

00:20:09.660 --> 00:20:12.500
Their names have no common characters...

00:20:12.160 --> 00:20:20.590
Chikara Oyamada (A Type)

00:20:12.160 --> 00:20:20.590
Born in year 31, Oct. Showa Era.

00:20:12.160 --> 00:20:20.590
Interest: Hot Spring Tour

00:20:12.160 --> 00:20:20.590
Sasuke Sorato (B Type)

00:20:12.160 --> 00:20:20.590
Born in year 32, June. Showa Era.

00:20:12.160 --> 00:20:20.590
Interest: Hang glider

00:20:12.160 --> 00:20:20.590
Futatsu Kokohari (O Type)

00:20:12.160 --> 00:20:20.590
Born in year 33, Jan. Showa Era.

00:20:12.160 --> 00:20:20.590
Interest: Walking

00:20:12.750 --> 00:20:17.590
Their birthdates and blood types are all different, as are their hobbies.

00:20:17.590 --> 00:20:20.130
This is harder than I thought...

00:20:21.050 --> 00:20:24.010
What could it be? Do you suppose they have something in common?

00:20:41.820 --> 00:20:45.950
I give up. I think I'll wait for the pro's answer.

00:20:45.950 --> 00:20:47.160
Same here...

00:20:50.580 --> 00:20:52.790
Do you think Dad'll be all right?

00:20:54.170 --> 00:20:57.630
<i>Wait, these three people</i> <i>were each born a year apart...</i>

00:21:01.170 --> 00:21:02.470
<i>I got it!</i>

00:21:02.880 --> 00:21:04.590
It's "Momotaro"!
<i>(famous folk tale hero)</i>

00:21:05.430 --> 00:21:07.350
M-Momotaro?!

00:21:07.350 --> 00:21:09.560
It's their Chinese zodiac signs!

00:21:09.560 --> 00:21:12.230
The years of the monkey, the rooster, and the dog...

00:21:12.310 --> 00:21:16.850
A monkey, a bird, and a dog were all Momotaro's retainers!

00:21:18.110 --> 00:21:21.110
Correct, little boy!
Most impressive!

00:21:24.780 --> 00:21:27.950
<i>Gotta have embarrassments</i> <i>sometimes too, old man!</i>

00:21:29.080 --> 00:21:31.160
Seeing as you've solved the puzzle,

00:21:31.160 --> 00:21:34.910
I'll give you a special tour of my gallery, Conan-<i>kun</i>!

00:21:35.370 --> 00:21:37.080
You may come too, Ran-<i>san</i>!

00:21:37.170 --> 00:21:38.000
Okay!

00:21:39.750 --> 00:21:41.880
Please feel free to look around!

00:21:53.140 --> 00:21:56.190
Huh? Ran-<i>neechan</i>!
Isn't this that one house?

00:21:58.600 --> 00:21:59.770
Oh, it is!

00:21:59.860 --> 00:22:01.570
It's Kurokawa-<i>san</i>'s mansion!

00:22:01.570 --> 00:22:04.990
Speaking of which, wasn't Kurokawa-<i>san</i> murdered?

00:22:05.070 --> 00:22:05.950
Yes...

00:22:06.320 --> 00:22:10.200
I designed this house very shortly after I struck out on my own.

00:22:10.530 --> 00:22:14.200
Everything beyond it is from my 30s.

00:22:16.120 --> 00:22:19.920
I was still inept in my youth.
Please don't pay them much attention...

00:22:20.130 --> 00:22:22.960
<i>He's even designed a bridge...</i>

00:22:23.130 --> 00:22:26.720
Incidentally, Ran-<i>san.</i>
Are you and Kudo-<i>kun</i> very close?

00:22:27.380 --> 00:22:28.760
Yes, I suppose!

00:22:29.010 --> 00:22:32.010
We grew up together, and we go to the same high school!

00:22:32.350 --> 00:22:34.680
Though I haven't seen him at all recently...

00:22:36.270 --> 00:22:38.730
But this Sunday, Shinichi...

00:22:38.730 --> 00:22:43.730
No, he and I have a date to see a movie on his birthday!

00:22:43.730 --> 00:22:46.570
Oh, that sounds like fun!

00:22:46.650 --> 00:22:49.360
I take it you've already gotten him a present?

00:22:49.360 --> 00:22:51.660
No, on Saturday
I'm going to...

00:22:51.740 --> 00:22:55.160
He and I both like the color red!

00:22:55.240 --> 00:22:58.410
And we both have red as our lucky color for May!

00:22:58.620 --> 00:23:02.040
So I was thinking of giving him a red polo shirt!

00:23:02.170 --> 00:23:07.470
That sounds like a marvelous present!
I'm sure Kudo-<i>kun</i> will love it!

00:23:07.550 --> 00:23:08.590
Thanks!

00:23:08.670 --> 00:23:12.680
<i>Crap! I haven't figured out</i> <i>what to do on my birthday!</i>

00:23:13.100 --> 00:23:16.850
Oh? Isn't this the Beika City Building?

00:23:16.930 --> 00:23:18.310
That's right.

00:23:18.640 --> 00:23:21.980
We're seeing the movie in this building, in Beika Cinema 1!

00:23:21.980 --> 00:23:24.610
We're meeting in the lobby at 10:00 on the night of the 3rd!

00:23:24.690 --> 00:23:29.110
Is that so? This building is one of my best works...

00:23:29.200 --> 00:23:34.700
There's no better place for a young couple to celebrate a birthday at!

00:23:34.830 --> 00:23:37.370
<i>W-what am I gonna do?</i>

00:23:38.540 --> 00:23:41.120
"May 3rd (Saturday)"

00:23:41.420 --> 00:23:44.130
Well, order something for dinner, okay?

00:23:44.130 --> 00:23:45.040
Okay...

00:23:45.420 --> 00:23:47.960
Ten hours until 10:00 at night...

00:23:48.090 --> 00:23:49.630
I am so screwed...

00:23:53.800 --> 00:23:55.390
See you later!

00:23:55.640 --> 00:23:58.220
What am I hiding for?

00:23:58.350 --> 00:24:01.520
I told you to turn her down earlier!

00:24:01.640 --> 00:24:03.310
I couldn't help it!

00:24:03.310 --> 00:24:06.650
I couldn't turn Ran down after seeing her check her calendar

00:24:06.650 --> 00:24:08.940
so happily everyday!

00:24:09.190 --> 00:24:12.450
Doc, build me a fancy Shinichi robot!

00:24:12.450 --> 00:24:16.080
I'm afraid that's not possible, even for a genius like me!

00:24:16.330 --> 00:24:17.580
Didn't think so...

00:24:18.330 --> 00:24:20.910
<i>Two days ago,</i> <i>a large amount of explosives,</i>

00:24:20.910 --> 00:24:24.000
<i>containing octogen, was stolen</i> <i>from a Toyo Munitions warehouse.</i>

00:24:24.080 --> 00:24:28.210
<i>The police have mobilized over</i> <i>100 officers for the investigation,</i>

00:24:28.210 --> 00:24:31.340
<i>but no clues have been found yet.</i>

00:24:30.130 --> 00:24:32.510
<i>Talk about scary...</i>

00:24:32.930 --> 00:24:37.680
Yeah. Octogen molded together with plastic makes plastic explosives.

00:24:37.680 --> 00:24:41.640
<i>Kurokawa mansion burned down,</i> <i>including several nearby houses.</i>

00:24:42.350 --> 00:24:44.730
That's the Kurokawa house from the other day!

00:24:44.730 --> 00:24:47.440
Yes, where that murder took place...

00:24:47.520 --> 00:24:50.690
There sure have been a lot of arsons lately...

00:24:51.900 --> 00:24:55.450
<i>the police believe the same person</i> <i>is responsible for this fire...</i>

00:24:56.740 --> 00:24:58.580
Yes, hello?

00:24:58.580 --> 00:25:00.330
Is Kudo Shinichi there?

00:25:00.580 --> 00:25:02.460
Just a minute.

00:25:02.710 --> 00:25:04.170
It's for you, Shinichi.

00:25:04.170 --> 00:25:06.210
How do they know I'm here?!

00:25:06.290 --> 00:25:13.590
Don't be silly! You know all calls to your house get routed here now!

00:25:13.840 --> 00:25:16.720
Oh, right! My bad...

00:25:16.840 --> 00:25:21.350
But I never get calls anymore, so I completely forgot.

00:25:21.470 --> 00:25:25.520
He sounds odd, as if he's using a voice changer too!

00:25:26.810 --> 00:25:27.900
Hello?

00:25:27.900 --> 00:25:29.270
Kudo Shinichi?

00:25:29.360 --> 00:25:30.070
Yes.

00:25:30.070 --> 00:25:34.030
You catch the news? I stole the explosives from Toyo Munitions!

00:25:34.030 --> 00:25:35.110
What?!

00:25:35.530 --> 00:25:38.700
Think you could give me your cell phone number?

00:25:39.200 --> 00:25:42.040
I have no obligation to give it to you!

00:25:42.040 --> 00:25:46.420
Oh, so you don't care if your only contact with me gets cut?

00:25:48.670 --> 00:25:50.500
Alright. The number is...

00:25:54.010 --> 00:25:58.550
Alright. Now take your phone and come to Green Park on the Teimuzu River.

00:25:58.550 --> 00:26:00.560
I have something interesting to show you!

00:26:01.310 --> 00:26:02.520
Green Park?!

00:26:02.520 --> 00:26:04.430
Better hurry before some kids die!

00:26:04.430 --> 00:26:05.350
What?!

00:26:06.640 --> 00:26:07.560
Shinichi!

00:26:07.650 --> 00:26:09.020
I gotta check it out!

00:26:09.110 --> 00:26:10.650
You sure it's not just a prank call?

00:26:10.730 --> 00:26:13.690
Using a voice changer is too much to be a prank!

00:26:14.030 --> 00:26:16.030
Contact Inspector Megure, Doc!

00:26:16.030 --> 00:26:17.740
Right! Be careful, now!

00:26:17.740 --> 00:26:19.030
Yeah, yeah!

00:26:42.140 --> 00:26:45.810
"Teimuzu River Green Park"

00:26:49.940 --> 00:26:53.570
"Genta"

00:26:49.940 --> 00:26:53.570
"Mitsuhiko"

00:26:49.940 --> 00:26:53.570
"Ayumi"

00:26:50.310 --> 00:26:52.820
C'mon, Mitsuhiko! Lemme fly it now!

00:26:52.480 --> 00:26:53.940
I want to try, too!

00:26:53.940 --> 00:26:55.650
Hold on a minute.

00:26:55.740 --> 00:26:59.240
Piloting a remote-control plane is quite tough...

00:26:59.320 --> 00:27:02.200
Hey, Mitsuhiko!
Where'd you get that plane?!

00:27:02.280 --> 00:27:03.280
Conan-<i>kun</i>!

00:27:03.280 --> 00:27:05.620
A man with a beard gave it to us!

00:27:05.620 --> 00:27:07.960
He said it was a bomber plane!

00:27:08.290 --> 00:27:09.790
A bomber plane?!

00:27:10.290 --> 00:27:12.710
<i>That thing beneath its fuselage...</i>

00:27:13.130 --> 00:27:14.460
<i>...could it be a bomb?!</i>

00:27:14.460 --> 00:27:18.340
- Gimme that, Mitsuhiko!

00:27:15.920 --> 00:27:18.340
- What?! It's my turn next!

00:27:18.470 --> 00:27:20.260
There's a bomb on that plane!

00:27:21.890 --> 00:27:22.970
You idiots!

00:27:23.100 --> 00:27:24.430
Oh no!

00:27:24.510 --> 00:27:26.020
The antenna broke off!

00:27:26.020 --> 00:27:27.520
Conan-<i>kun</i>! The plane!

00:27:29.690 --> 00:27:31.730
It's no use!
Everyone, run!

00:27:32.940 --> 00:27:34.820
You idiots!
Not that way!

00:27:36.150 --> 00:27:37.820
Conan! Do something!

00:27:37.900 --> 00:27:38.860
Damn it!

00:27:45.870 --> 00:27:46.910
Not good!

00:27:49.040 --> 00:27:50.210
Go!

00:27:59.380 --> 00:28:01.720
- What blew up?

00:28:00.880 --> 00:28:01.720
- Fireworks?

00:28:01.720 --> 00:28:03.470
It was a plane!

00:28:04.930 --> 00:28:08.020
An orange flash!
Plastic explosives!

00:28:13.230 --> 00:28:14.610
What's the big idea?!

00:28:14.610 --> 00:28:15.900
Where's Kudo?

00:28:15.980 --> 00:28:17.070
<i>Crap!</i>

00:28:17.070 --> 00:28:21.150
Ah, so he's saying a brat like you is enough to handle me...

00:28:21.780 --> 00:28:23.030
<i>"Like you"?</i>

00:28:23.240 --> 00:28:24.990
<i>Is he watching me from somewhere?!</i>

00:28:28.160 --> 00:28:29.330
Alright, listen up!

00:28:29.450 --> 00:28:32.210
In exactly one hour, another bomb will explode!

00:28:32.460 --> 00:28:33.870
Exactly one hour?!

00:28:34.420 --> 00:28:36.290
In the plaza in front of Beika Station!

00:28:36.630 --> 00:28:39.460
If Kudo won't come, then you find it!

00:28:40.010 --> 00:28:43.880
Wait! I'm just a kid.
I can't find it that easy!

00:28:43.970 --> 00:28:45.510
Gimme a hint or something!

00:28:46.220 --> 00:28:47.390
Hello?

00:28:47.810 --> 00:28:51.640
Beneath a tree. But it's not exactly buried beneath one.

00:28:51.770 --> 00:28:55.100
You better hurry, or someone might wind up taking it!

00:28:58.020 --> 00:28:59.110
Damn it!

00:28:59.480 --> 00:29:00.440
Conan-<i>kun</i>!

00:29:00.440 --> 00:29:02.740
Hey, Conan!
Where are you going?!

00:29:21.380 --> 00:29:22.720
<i>Ten to 1:00!</i>

00:29:31.350 --> 00:29:33.310
<i>No luck!</i>
<i>Can't find anything!</i>

00:29:43.570 --> 00:29:44.610
Welcome!

00:29:50.490 --> 00:29:52.700
<i>What does "under a tree" mean?!</i>

00:29:52.830 --> 00:29:55.000
<i>And what does he mean</i> <i>that someone'll take it?!</i>

00:30:00.670 --> 00:30:03.300
"Please, someone take her."

00:30:05.590 --> 00:30:09.640
Did someone abandon you?
You poor thing...

00:30:09.760 --> 00:30:13.680
Don't worry!
I'll take care of you!

00:30:16.230 --> 00:30:19.610
<i>Roots (nekko) are beneath a tree...</i>

00:30:19.900 --> 00:30:20.900
<i>A cat (neko)?!</i>

00:30:24.030 --> 00:30:25.360
Thank you!

00:30:25.570 --> 00:30:26.400
Huh?

00:30:29.410 --> 00:30:31.120
Wait, old lady!

00:30:32.740 --> 00:30:35.330
You idiot!
Can't you see the stoplight?!

00:30:35.330 --> 00:30:36.750
S-sorry!

00:30:39.380 --> 00:30:40.790
Oh no!

00:30:41.170 --> 00:30:42.500
Five minutes to 1:00!

00:30:42.590 --> 00:30:43.550
Dammit!

00:30:59.560 --> 00:31:01.110
Four minutes to 1:00!

00:31:04.530 --> 00:31:06.820
Alright! She's caught in traffic!

00:31:07.030 --> 00:31:10.030
What's going on?!
The sun is still high up...

00:31:10.240 --> 00:31:14.290
Oh, yeah! It must've broken somewhere when it went flying!

00:31:20.540 --> 00:31:22.590
I'm borrowin' your bike, kid!

00:31:22.590 --> 00:31:23.670
Wait!

00:31:25.500 --> 00:31:28.840
Huh? "Kid"?
I'm younger than him?!

00:31:32.550 --> 00:31:34.470
Oh no! It's starting to move!

00:31:34.640 --> 00:31:35.970
Three minutes to 1:00!

00:31:36.270 --> 00:31:40.140
Hey, yeah! This road makes a big curve to the left!

00:31:52.910 --> 00:31:55.120
A-are you alright, kid?!

00:31:55.530 --> 00:31:57.240
Gimme this case, old lady!

00:32:00.500 --> 00:32:01.870
25 seconds left!

00:32:02.000 --> 00:32:03.790
Hey, kid! Are you alright?!

00:32:03.790 --> 00:32:04.540
Yeah...

00:32:04.630 --> 00:32:05.590
<i>Damn!</i>

00:32:05.590 --> 00:32:08.630
<i>I can't let it detonate here!</i>
<i>What do I do?!</i>

00:32:11.380 --> 00:32:13.430
<i>It stopped?! Alright!</i>

00:32:14.430 --> 00:32:16.850
<i>I'm pretty sure there's</i> <i>an empty lot past the freeway!</i>

00:32:20.560 --> 00:32:21.940
You don't need this?

00:32:26.320 --> 00:32:27.570
It's ticking again!

00:33:02.180 --> 00:33:06.100
"Suzuki Sonoko - Teitan High School Junior"

00:33:02.690 --> 00:33:04.400
Yeah, this is the one!

00:33:04.480 --> 00:33:06.480
Ooh, how flashy!

00:33:06.480 --> 00:33:07.900
But this color is...

00:33:06.940 --> 00:33:11.650
<i>After being injured trying to distance</i> <i>the device from people's homes,</i>

00:33:11.740 --> 00:33:15.320
<i>the boy was rushed to the police hospital,</i> <i>where he is being treated.</i>

00:33:33.720 --> 00:33:35.340
Conan-<i>kun</i>! You're awake!

00:33:35.340 --> 00:33:37.220
Conan! You okay?!

00:33:38.720 --> 00:33:40.720
- Where am I?

00:33:39.510 --> 00:33:40.720
- The hospital!

00:33:40.850 --> 00:33:43.430
Conan! What the hell were you doing?!

00:33:43.520 --> 00:33:44.680
Now, now...

00:33:43.980 --> 00:33:46.060
Explain so I can understand!

00:33:46.140 --> 00:33:48.980
Your questions can wait!

00:33:46.140 --> 00:33:48.980
Go get the doctor!

00:33:48.650 --> 00:33:49.650
Conan!

00:33:49.060 --> 00:33:49.770
I'll get him!

00:33:49.770 --> 00:33:51.030
Calm down!

00:34:00.160 --> 00:34:00.990
Right.

00:34:01.160 --> 00:34:02.870
Nothing to worry about now.

00:34:02.950 --> 00:34:06.830
His brain waves were just fine when we checked earlier,

00:34:07.250 --> 00:34:09.080
so he can probably leave tomorrow.

00:34:09.420 --> 00:34:11.170
Thank you...

00:34:12.710 --> 00:34:13.590
Take care.

00:34:13.670 --> 00:34:14.970
Take care of yourself.

00:34:18.140 --> 00:34:22.220
Sorry to be sudden, Conan-<i>kun,</i> but can you tell us what happened?!

00:34:22.310 --> 00:34:23.270
Yeah!

00:34:26.690 --> 00:34:27.810
I see...

00:34:27.900 --> 00:34:33.030
So you rode the bike to protect others from the explosion?

00:34:33.110 --> 00:34:33.900
Yeah...

00:34:33.900 --> 00:34:35.150
Oh, Inspector!

00:34:36.360 --> 00:34:40.950
The culprit makes contact by calling
Shinichi-<i>niichan</i>'s cell phone!

00:34:41.030 --> 00:34:43.790
But you can't use cell phones in hospitals...

00:34:43.790 --> 00:34:45.830
Oh, there's no need to worry.

00:34:46.040 --> 00:34:49.000
We're isolated from that ward there,

00:34:49.080 --> 00:34:52.040
and there are no electronic medical devices here,

00:34:52.290 --> 00:34:55.510
so cell phones can be used here!

00:34:56.090 --> 00:34:59.720
Dr. Agasa explained the situation, which is why we brought you here!

00:35:00.390 --> 00:35:01.550
That's a relief...

00:35:01.850 --> 00:35:05.220
Also, I ruined that bicycle...

00:35:05.220 --> 00:35:07.890
Could you pay for it later, mister?

00:35:08.060 --> 00:35:12.060
Never mind that, why did you do something so reckless?!

00:35:12.150 --> 00:35:14.900
You nearly died, you know!

00:35:14.900 --> 00:35:15.900
Sorry...

00:35:16.030 --> 00:35:21.950
Anyways, where is Shinichi?!
The guy's trying to call him, right?!

00:35:22.030 --> 00:35:24.700
As I said, Shinichi-<i>kun</i> is busy with something else,

00:35:24.700 --> 00:35:27.200
so he asked Conan-<i>kun</i> to handle this...

00:35:27.330 --> 00:35:31.080
What a lowlife! I'll teach him a lesson next time I see him!

00:35:31.880 --> 00:35:35.420
<i>Definitely can't tell him</i>
<i>I'm Kudo Shinichi...</i>

00:35:37.010 --> 00:35:40.260
Anyway, Inspector! Did you find out what kind of bombs they were?!

00:35:40.380 --> 00:35:41.260
Yes.

00:35:41.260 --> 00:35:46.970
Both the plane and the carrying case bombs used plastic explosives.

00:35:47.850 --> 00:35:49.020
<i>Just as I thought...</i>

00:35:55.480 --> 00:35:59.780
<i>A blue-tinged, orange flash is the</i> <i>telltale sign of a plastic explosive!</i>

00:36:01.240 --> 00:36:05.200
They were most likely explosives stolen from Toyo Munitions.

00:36:05.280 --> 00:36:09.370
The plane had a concussion bomb with a detonator cap attached,

00:36:10.160 --> 00:36:15.090
while the carrying case had a time bomb connected to a timer.

00:36:15.540 --> 00:36:20.800
But the fact it temporarily stopped 16 seconds before 1:00 bugs me...

00:36:20.880 --> 00:36:22.760
About that...

00:36:23.050 --> 00:36:26.850
The only possibilities are that the timer stopped due to a malfunction,

00:36:26.850 --> 00:36:34.350
or that the culprit stopped it remotely for whatever reason...

00:36:34.690 --> 00:36:38.190
From the fact that the culprit went out of his way to phone Kudo-<i>kun,</i>

00:36:38.320 --> 00:36:43.320
he either wanted to challenge the famous high school detective,

00:36:43.610 --> 00:36:46.990
or he's someone with a personal grudge against him.

00:36:47.240 --> 00:36:48.660
From what I've looked into,

00:36:49.120 --> 00:36:52.040
all the criminals from cases solved by Kudo Shinichi-<i>kun</i>

00:36:52.120 --> 00:36:55.080
are currently serving out their prison sentences.

00:36:55.080 --> 00:36:58.090
Meaning it must be a relative or lover...

00:36:58.170 --> 00:37:03.840
In any case, we're out looking for the man from the sketch they drew.

00:37:03.930 --> 00:37:06.510
He means this, Conan!
It looks just like him!

00:37:06.510 --> 00:37:09.680
- It's a work of art!

00:37:07.680 --> 00:37:09.680
- We all drew it together!

00:37:10.890 --> 00:37:13.890
You really got his main features!

00:37:14.100 --> 00:37:16.020
<i>But it doesn't ring any bells...</i>

00:37:16.730 --> 00:37:19.230
<i>He used a voice changer</i> <i>to alter his voice!</i>

00:37:20.610 --> 00:37:23.490
<i>It could be someone I know!</i>

00:37:24.240 --> 00:37:28.120
Inspector. Out of all of Shinichi-<i>kun</i>'s cases so far,

00:37:28.120 --> 00:37:31.830
which one received the most public attention?

00:37:34.370 --> 00:37:40.500
That'd be the one involving
Mayor Okamoto of West Tama City...

00:37:41.760 --> 00:37:45.220
A 25 year old female office worker living in West Tama City died

00:37:45.340 --> 00:37:50.010
when she was hit by a car the mayor's son was driving.

00:38:04.650 --> 00:38:07.570
The mayor had been in the passenger seat

00:38:07.570 --> 00:38:10.620
during what at first seemed to be a regular accident...

00:38:11.490 --> 00:38:14.870
...but Kudo-<i>kun</i> was skeptical about it.

00:38:11.870 --> 00:38:14.870
"Kudo Shinichi - Teitan High School Junior"

00:38:17.080 --> 00:38:20.040
"Okamoto Shicho (52)

00:38:17.080 --> 00:38:20.040
"Okamoto Kohei (21)

00:38:17.080 --> 00:38:20.040
Mayor's Son"

00:38:17.080 --> 00:38:20.040
West Tama City Mayor"

00:38:30.300 --> 00:38:34.930
This cigarette butt was found lying directly next to the victim.

00:38:35.390 --> 00:38:37.600
The son's saliva was found on it.

00:38:37.940 --> 00:38:39.440
So you tossed this away?

00:38:39.440 --> 00:38:41.020
Y-yes.

00:38:41.270 --> 00:38:45.400
After I hit her, I rushed out of the driver's seat and over to her.

00:38:45.570 --> 00:38:48.660
I probably unconsciously threw it away then.

00:38:51.370 --> 00:38:52.490
I see.

00:38:52.580 --> 00:38:57.160
Judging from its length, it hadn't been lit for very long at all.

00:38:57.250 --> 00:38:59.710
Yes, it happened just after I lit it.

00:38:59.830 --> 00:39:01.460
- With a lighter?
- Yes.

00:39:01.590 --> 00:39:03.500
What lighter did you use?

00:39:04.050 --> 00:39:05.840
The car's cigarette lighter.

00:39:07.050 --> 00:39:11.470
Then please get in the driver's seat and try lighting a cigarette!

00:39:16.600 --> 00:39:18.270
You need only go through the actions.

00:39:21.480 --> 00:39:24.570
But... with your seatbelt on, please.

00:39:24.650 --> 00:39:25.530
Okay.

00:39:28.360 --> 00:39:29.450
Here...

00:39:30.160 --> 00:39:31.820
Use one of these.

00:39:32.780 --> 00:39:36.160
They're the same kind as the one found at the scene.

00:39:36.330 --> 00:39:37.290
Alright...

00:39:46.210 --> 00:39:47.210
Stop!

00:39:48.090 --> 00:39:48.920
Yes...

00:39:49.010 --> 00:39:53.800
The only way to reach it from the driver's seat is with your left hand.

00:39:54.260 --> 00:39:59.100
But that lighter only had fingerprints from your right hand on it.

00:39:59.850 --> 00:40:02.560
How do you explain that, Kohei-<i>san</i>?

00:40:02.810 --> 00:40:04.980
I must've used my own lighter to...

00:40:04.980 --> 00:40:06.070
Nope.

00:40:07.690 --> 00:40:11.780
You accidentally left this lighter where you had just been.

00:40:11.990 --> 00:40:15.080
And your father doesn't smoke...

00:40:18.080 --> 00:40:23.580
You unquestionably used this car's lighter from the passenger seat...

00:40:23.880 --> 00:40:26.670
...as your father sat next to you, driving!

00:40:28.130 --> 00:40:31.510
All other fingerprints were craftily replaced...

00:40:31.880 --> 00:40:35.550
Even the seat positions and mirror angles were perfect...

00:40:35.720 --> 00:40:42.640
But it seems you overlooked the cigarette lighter, Mayor Okamoto...

00:40:47.480 --> 00:40:55.370
My son, Kohei, volunteered to take my place to save my position...

00:40:56.660 --> 00:41:00.000
I was really the one driving!

00:41:00.660 --> 00:41:02.580
I'm so very sorry!

00:41:05.500 --> 00:41:06.630
<i>Dad...</i>

00:41:09.880 --> 00:41:13.430
As a result of that incident,
Mayor Okamoto lost his position,

00:41:13.720 --> 00:41:19.970
and his plans for a revitalized
West Tama City were scrapped.

00:41:22.600 --> 00:41:27.310
Inspector. Do you suppose his son holds a grudge for what happened?

00:41:27.560 --> 00:41:33.820
Come to think of it, he was an electrical engineering student...

00:41:33.820 --> 00:41:34.990
I'll look into it!

00:41:38.160 --> 00:41:42.290
Do you remember anything else about the culprit?

00:41:42.290 --> 00:41:43.910
Anything at all...

00:41:46.670 --> 00:41:48.630
Hmm...

00:41:51.000 --> 00:41:52.210
A smell...

00:41:53.550 --> 00:41:58.600
There was this sweet smell when he gave Mitsuhiko-<i>kun</i> the plane...

00:41:58.760 --> 00:42:02.220
There was?
I didn't notice anything!

00:42:02.220 --> 00:42:03.560
Me neither...

00:42:03.770 --> 00:42:06.690
Could the sweet smell have been from cosmetics or something?

00:42:07.150 --> 00:42:12.320
I don't know. But it seemed different from perfume...

00:42:13.070 --> 00:42:14.530
<i>A sweet smell?</i>

00:42:15.240 --> 00:42:19.320
Alright. If you remember anything, let me know.

00:42:19.320 --> 00:42:21.330
We will!

00:42:21.580 --> 00:42:24.700
Well, we should probably get going...

00:42:24.790 --> 00:42:28.080
Yeah. Conan is all better now...

00:42:29.750 --> 00:42:32.920
If anything bad happens,
I'll rush straight here!

00:42:33.050 --> 00:42:34.970
Y-yeah, thanks...

00:42:35.170 --> 00:42:36.720
He's so lucky...

00:42:36.800 --> 00:42:39.300
We should get hospitalized, too!

00:42:39.300 --> 00:42:43.560
You certainly are popular with the girls, lover-boy!

00:42:45.060 --> 00:42:47.020
<i>He has no idea how to read people...</i>

00:42:47.640 --> 00:42:49.730
Well, bye!

00:42:49.810 --> 00:42:50.980
See ya, Conan!

00:42:50.980 --> 00:42:52.150
Thanks!

00:42:52.650 --> 00:42:57.530
Still, where could Kudo-<i>kun</i> have gone at such an important time?!

00:43:05.200 --> 00:43:06.330
Wait, Conan!

00:43:06.450 --> 00:43:08.960
Listen. If it's the bomber,
I'll handle him!

00:43:11.330 --> 00:43:12.340
Hello?

00:43:12.460 --> 00:43:15.670
I'm impressed you found the bombs. Well done.

00:43:15.800 --> 00:43:19.630
But children's time is over.
Put Kudo on!

00:43:21.640 --> 00:43:24.720
Yes, now it's adult time!

00:43:24.810 --> 00:43:27.100
Who's this?!
Where's Kudo?!

00:43:27.270 --> 00:43:31.610
Kudo isn't here!
Now you're dealing with me!

00:43:31.940 --> 00:43:35.320
The great detective, Mori Kogoro!

00:43:36.230 --> 00:43:40.280
Fine. Now listen close;
I'll only say this once!

00:43:40.490 --> 00:43:43.410
I've planted five bombs on the Touto Loop Line!

00:43:44.700 --> 00:43:45.950
Five...

00:43:46.040 --> 00:43:47.080
bombs?!

00:43:51.370 --> 00:43:58.260
If any trains travel below 60 kph after 4:00 pm, the bombs'll blow.

00:43:58.420 --> 00:44:04.010
They're also set to explode if not dismantled by sundown.

00:44:04.180 --> 00:44:05.850
I'll give you just one hint...

00:44:08.100 --> 00:44:13.060
The bombs are planted "X the X" on the Touto Loop Line.

00:44:13.650 --> 00:44:16.570
In each "X" goes one word.

00:44:16.730 --> 00:44:19.990
Well, good luck,
Great Detective Mori.

00:44:24.870 --> 00:44:29.450
H-he's just bluffing!
Planting bombs on the Loop...

00:44:29.450 --> 00:44:31.580
No, he means business.

00:44:31.710 --> 00:44:35.710
He most likely has the detonators set for 4:00 pm,

00:44:36.040 --> 00:44:42.050
and if the trains fall below 60 kph after that... they'll explode.

00:44:44.680 --> 00:44:47.760
In any case,
I need to contact HQ...

00:44:50.730 --> 00:44:51.980
It's Megure...

00:44:52.520 --> 00:44:55.230
<i>I agree with Inspector Megure...</i>

00:44:57.440 --> 00:45:04.110
<i>But what exactly is the bomber after?!</i>
<i>Why do something like this?!</i>

00:45:17.840 --> 00:45:19.590
Just made it!

00:45:19.590 --> 00:45:21.210
Today's our lucky day!

00:45:24.010 --> 00:45:26.970
"Touto Railway Terminal Station"

00:45:24.930 --> 00:45:27.470
Bombs on the Loop?!

00:45:26.970 --> 00:45:30.890
"Touto Railway Traffic Control Room"

00:45:27.550 --> 00:45:30.520
We just received emergency contact from the police department!

00:45:30.640 --> 00:45:33.640
Understood! I'll stop all trains at once and have them inspected!

00:45:33.140 --> 00:45:40.400
"Command Chief

00:45:33.140 --> 00:45:40.400
"Traffic Dept. Head

00:45:33.140 --> 00:45:40.400
Sakaguchi (52)"

00:45:33.140 --> 00:45:40.400
Kusunoki (45)"

00:45:33.690 --> 00:45:35.810
No! We can't stop them!

00:45:36.440 --> 00:45:44.030
The bombs'll explode if the trains go below 60 kph after 4:00 pm!

00:45:45.160 --> 00:45:46.410
Say what?!

00:45:48.320 --> 00:45:50.580
There's only three minutes until 4:00!

00:45:50.700 --> 00:45:58.290
Order all trains on the Loop to travel above 60, no, 70 kph!

00:45:58.420 --> 00:46:00.380
What about the trains stopped at stations?!

00:46:00.380 --> 00:46:01.840
Get them moving immediately!

00:46:01.960 --> 00:46:03.550
What about trains about to stop?

00:46:03.550 --> 00:46:04.760
Send them through!

00:46:04.880 --> 00:46:07.550
All we can do is keep all the trains running nonstop

00:46:07.550 --> 00:46:09.800
until the bombs are found!

00:46:09.890 --> 00:46:10.760
Kusunoki-<i>kun</i>!

00:46:10.850 --> 00:46:11.930
U-understood!

00:46:13.850 --> 00:46:16.270
Emergency orders!
Emergency orders!

00:46:16.350 --> 00:46:19.650
Attention, all trains!
Someone has planted bombs!

00:46:19.770 --> 00:46:22.280
They'll explode if they're traveling under 60 kph!

00:46:22.440 --> 00:46:24.490
All trains are to stay at 70 kph!

00:46:24.490 --> 00:46:27.530
I repeat, someone has planted bombs!

00:46:27.530 --> 00:46:29.570
They'll explode if they're traveling under 60 kph!

00:46:29.570 --> 00:46:31.660
All trains are to stay at 70 kph!

00:46:34.370 --> 00:46:36.790
Hey, doesn't this train seem strange?

00:46:36.790 --> 00:46:38.370
How so, Genta-<i>kun</i>?

00:46:38.540 --> 00:46:43.210
We're almost to Beika Station, but we're slowly speeding up...

00:46:44.050 --> 00:46:45.800
Attention, passengers.

00:46:45.920 --> 00:46:50.430
Due to an emergency, this train will pass through Beika Station.

00:46:51.810 --> 00:46:54.310
Hey! What does "emergency" mean?

00:46:55.560 --> 00:47:02.690
Due to an emergency, the train on Line #1 will be passing through.

00:47:08.280 --> 00:47:10.700
I see! Alright!

00:47:10.910 --> 00:47:14.290
Apparently, no trains have exploded so far.

00:47:15.370 --> 00:47:17.790
I've got it, Inspector Megure!

00:47:17.960 --> 00:47:19.790
Got what?

00:47:19.960 --> 00:47:26.130
"X the X" means "beneath the seats", or "above the racks"!

00:47:26.300 --> 00:47:28.760
That's where the bombs are!

00:47:28.880 --> 00:47:32.470
"Under the trains" is also a possibility.

00:47:32.470 --> 00:47:34.970
Yes, well...

00:47:35.220 --> 00:47:39.890
Say, weren't Ayumi-<i>kun</i> and the others getting on the Loop Line

00:47:39.980 --> 00:47:43.480
from Midoridai Station to get back to Beika?

00:47:46.400 --> 00:47:51.320
Again, this train will continue to run nonstop for the time being.

00:47:51.450 --> 00:47:54.080
Should you find a suspicious item onboard,

00:47:54.080 --> 00:47:57.290
please refrain from touching it and let the conductor know.

00:47:57.870 --> 00:48:00.460
W-what does "suspicious item" mean?!

00:48:00.460 --> 00:48:02.130
He means something out of the ordinary!

00:48:02.210 --> 00:48:05.130
I know that! But what's "out of the ordinary"?!

00:48:05.130 --> 00:48:07.050
Well, that would be, uhh...

00:48:07.130 --> 00:48:08.550
Ayumi-<i>chan</i>, do you read me?!

00:48:08.630 --> 00:48:10.510
Conan-<i>kun</i>! I read you!

00:48:10.630 --> 00:48:12.010
Where are you right now?!

00:48:12.090 --> 00:48:13.600
On the Loop...

00:48:15.600 --> 00:48:16.560
I thought so...

00:48:16.640 --> 00:48:19.980
Hey, Conan! What in the world's goin' on?

00:48:19.980 --> 00:48:23.900
Don't tell us there's something that starts with a "b" on the train?!

00:48:25.320 --> 00:48:27.610
Don't worry, it's nothin'!

00:48:27.610 --> 00:48:32.860
Look! There's no guarantee the bombs are only inside the trains!

00:48:33.950 --> 00:48:36.030
- Bombs?!

00:48:34.950 --> 00:48:36.030
- I knew it!

00:48:36.410 --> 00:48:39.160
Does that mean we're gonna die?!

00:48:39.250 --> 00:48:42.290
Of course not!
I will find where they're hidden!

00:48:44.040 --> 00:48:45.130
Conan-<i>kun...</i>

00:48:47.340 --> 00:48:50.470
Darn it! We can't leave this all to Conan-<i>kun</i>!

00:48:50.470 --> 00:48:54.720
We gotta try hard, too! This calls for the Junior Detective League!

00:48:54.720 --> 00:48:55.640
The Junior...

00:48:55.640 --> 00:48:57.010
...Detective League?

00:48:58.390 --> 00:49:02.640
Y-you're right! The bombs do seem to be inside the trains!

00:49:04.270 --> 00:49:08.070
Alright! Let's go,
Junior Detective League!

00:49:08.070 --> 00:49:09.230
Yeah!

00:49:09.230 --> 00:49:10.820
W-wait, you guys!

00:49:11.030 --> 00:49:13.110
They cut me off!

00:49:13.200 --> 00:49:15.030
They gonna be alright?!

00:49:15.160 --> 00:49:16.990
Alright! Got it!

00:49:18.080 --> 00:49:21.040
A joint task force has been assembled at HQ.

00:49:21.830 --> 00:49:24.620
I'm off to Touto Railways' command center.

00:49:24.750 --> 00:49:26.210
Will you come too?

00:49:27.090 --> 00:49:28.630
Yes! I will accompany you!

00:49:31.550 --> 00:49:33.720
It's just past 4:30!

00:49:34.180 --> 00:49:38.140
Look! All trains on the Touto Loop Line have continued to run nonstop

00:49:38.140 --> 00:49:41.390
for over half an hour!

00:49:46.190 --> 00:49:49.940
Both Touto Railways and the police department have only commented

00:49:50.070 --> 00:49:54.360
by saying that there has been an emergency situation!

00:49:55.910 --> 00:49:59.580
<i>3o minutes is the most the police</i> <i>can keep it under wraps...</i>

00:50:05.620 --> 00:50:09.920
Borrowed this from a nurse!
It'd be best to watch from your room.

00:50:17.930 --> 00:50:23.810
<i>Rigging them to explode if they</i> <i>go under 6o kph makes some sense...</i>

00:50:24.730 --> 00:50:29.690
<i>...but having them explode if they're</i> <i>not dismantled before sundown?</i>

00:50:30.520 --> 00:50:32.230
<i>What's that about?</i>

00:50:33.530 --> 00:50:36.030
<i>Why would they blow up</i> <i>when the sun sets?</i>

00:50:37.280 --> 00:50:39.660
<i>Does it have something to do</i> <i>with the trains' lights?</i>

00:50:48.620 --> 00:50:50.210
Here you are!

00:50:53.630 --> 00:50:54.960
Please enjoy!

00:50:56.420 --> 00:51:00.340
That outfit's pretty sweet!
You look good in red!

00:51:00.470 --> 00:51:01.600
Thanks!

00:51:01.850 --> 00:51:05.060
Both Shinichi and I have red as our lucky color this month!

00:51:06.430 --> 00:51:10.440
Come to think of it, I haven't seen
Shinichi-<i>kun</i> in a while either...

00:51:10.560 --> 00:51:12.770
Maybe I should go with you too!

00:51:12.770 --> 00:51:19.530
But it's going to be a boring movie, plus he's pretty boring himself...

00:51:19.530 --> 00:51:24.160
I'm just kidding! No one's gonna get in your guys' way!

00:51:24.370 --> 00:51:28.080
You get serious so easily, Ran!
That's why I love teasin' ya!

00:51:28.160 --> 00:51:30.040
You're so silly, Sonoko...

00:51:30.290 --> 00:51:34.300
But I'm surprised your dad's letting you go to an all-night movie!

00:51:34.380 --> 00:51:37.590
He was against it, but I ignored him!

00:51:37.970 --> 00:51:44.470
I bet he and Conan-<i>kun</i> are discussing dinner right about now!

00:51:47.680 --> 00:51:51.980
So you couldn't find anything suspicious inside the trains?!

00:51:51.980 --> 00:51:52.900
That's right...

00:51:53.310 --> 00:51:59.030
All 21 trains were thoroughly searched by their conductors,

00:51:59.030 --> 00:52:01.660
but all items had owners!

00:52:01.780 --> 00:52:03.240
So, how about your end?

00:52:03.320 --> 00:52:09.830
Videos taken along the tracks showed no bombs under the train cars.

00:52:09.910 --> 00:52:11.170
I see...

00:52:11.170 --> 00:52:13.670
Then where could the bombs be?!

00:52:13.750 --> 00:52:16.800
Bad news, sir!
The passengers are getting unruly!

00:52:19.550 --> 00:52:21.300
How long're you gonna keep this thing going?!

00:52:21.300 --> 00:52:22.640
Just stop it already!

00:52:22.720 --> 00:52:26.970
My child has a stomachache!
Please, let us get off!

00:52:28.850 --> 00:52:32.480
What is this "suspicious item" anyway?!
Don't tell me it's a bomb?!

00:52:32.560 --> 00:52:33.690
A-a bomb?!

00:52:33.690 --> 00:52:36.020
Screw this! I'm gettin' off!

00:52:35.440 --> 00:52:37.020
<i>Please stop it, sir!</i>

00:52:37.020 --> 00:52:40.530
- Calm down, sir! Stop!
- You'll get serious injured if jumping off!

00:52:40.650 --> 00:52:42.610
Chief Director! I can't keep this up!

00:52:42.700 --> 00:52:44.490
Hang in there a little longer!

00:52:44.570 --> 00:52:49.040
Mori-<i>kun</i>! Have you figured out any way to locate the bombs?!

00:52:51.750 --> 00:52:55.040
An hour and a half until sunset...

00:52:57.460 --> 00:53:00.970
Still, having them go off when the sun sets...

00:53:00.970 --> 00:53:04.180
That's like the exact opposite of my skateboard...

00:53:05.470 --> 00:53:10.680
You know, it's solar-powered, so it doesn't work once the sun sets.

00:53:11.480 --> 00:53:13.350
The sun?

00:53:15.440 --> 00:53:17.400
I got it!
I got it, Doc!

00:53:26.740 --> 00:53:27.780
Megure here!

00:53:27.780 --> 00:53:29.080
Inspector! It's Kudo!

00:53:29.160 --> 00:53:32.040
Oh! Kudo-<i>kun</i>!
I've been waiting!

00:53:32.290 --> 00:53:34.790
Dr. Agasa explained everything!

00:53:35.250 --> 00:53:39.500
The bombs are not "below the seats",

00:53:39.590 --> 00:53:42.840
"above the racks", or "under the trains"!

00:53:43.630 --> 00:53:45.260
They're "between the tracks"!

00:53:45.550 --> 00:53:47.180
Between the tracks?!

00:53:47.390 --> 00:53:53.430
The bombs are set to detonate after a dozen or so seconds of darkness!

00:53:53.980 --> 00:53:59.900
When the trains pass over, the cars block the light for a few seconds!

00:54:00.360 --> 00:54:04.320
One car is 20 meters in length; 10 cars is 200 meters long.

00:54:05.070 --> 00:54:08.700
60 kilometers per hour is 16.7 meters per second.

00:54:08.700 --> 00:54:12.830
In other words, it takes about 12 seconds to travel 200 meters!

00:54:13.250 --> 00:54:18.500
The bombs are rigged to explode just barely after that amount of time!

00:54:20.380 --> 00:54:24.010
So move the trains onto other lines immediately!

00:54:24.220 --> 00:54:27.930
There's no danger in stopping them as long as they're off the Loop!

00:54:28.010 --> 00:54:29.430
Understood!

00:54:29.930 --> 00:54:32.720
Mr. Sakaguchi.
You heard what to do!

00:54:32.720 --> 00:54:33.770
Right!

00:54:39.860 --> 00:54:44.530
Divert Train #11 onto the Shibahama
Station cargo line in 3 minutes!

00:54:44.650 --> 00:54:45.990
Get everything ready!

00:54:46.530 --> 00:54:50.070
Train #11, Train #11!
Track switch in three minutes!

00:54:50.200 --> 00:54:52.830
Shibahama Station, circuit confirm interlock on!

00:54:52.910 --> 00:54:55.080
Move all cargo trains onto emergency sidetracks!

00:54:55.330 --> 00:54:57.370
Train #11, passing through
Kawashina Station!

00:54:56.910 --> 00:54:59.830
"Shibahama Station"

00:54:57.620 --> 00:54:59.710
Train #10, passing through
Shibahama Station!

00:54:59.790 --> 00:55:01.080
Switching track!

00:55:15.390 --> 00:55:17.270
Reducing speed, now!

00:55:20.150 --> 00:55:22.860
68 kph... 66 kph...

00:55:23.190 --> 00:55:25.820
64... 63 kph...

00:55:26.030 --> 00:55:28.650
62... 61...

00:55:28.900 --> 00:55:30.200
60 kph!

00:55:31.120 --> 00:55:33.450
59! 58 kph!

00:55:33.530 --> 00:55:34.660
Everything normal?!

00:55:34.660 --> 00:55:36.370
Yes! All normal!

00:55:36.620 --> 00:55:40.580
Alright! Keep slowing and stop at the next cargo station!

00:55:40.580 --> 00:55:41.960
Roger that!

00:55:42.170 --> 00:55:43.460
We did it!

00:55:43.540 --> 00:55:48.970
No, we can't rest easy yet!
There are still 20 more trains on the Loop!

00:55:56.470 --> 00:56:10.470
<i>I sadly watched the rain</i> <i>pound on you as you bent over</i>

00:56:11.240 --> 00:56:25.290
<i>If there was only one umbrella</i> <i>in this world, I'd find it for you</i>

00:56:13.370 --> 00:56:14.950
Train #9! All normal!

00:56:15.030 --> 00:56:16.950
Train #20! All normal!

00:56:17.370 --> 00:56:18.870
One train left!

00:56:26.040 --> 00:56:39.020
<i>I can't do anything, but I can't</i> <i>get drenched in your place, either</i>

00:56:31.840 --> 00:56:36.430
This is Train #10!
Currently at 55 kph! All normal here!

00:56:36.850 --> 00:56:39.020
We did it!

00:56:40.600 --> 00:56:52.030
<i>I beg of you,</i> <i>please confess your worries to me</i>

00:56:40.600 --> 00:56:43.190
We did it! We did it!
We pulled it off!

00:56:43.230 --> 00:56:46.110
A truly excellent display of skill!

00:56:46.110 --> 00:56:47.780
Excellent work!

00:56:47.820 --> 00:56:50.240
Now it's our turn to handle things!

00:56:55.320 --> 00:56:57.540
Whew, we finally managed to get off!

00:56:57.620 --> 00:57:00.660
I'm never rushing onto a train last-minute again!

00:57:01.120 --> 00:57:02.920
Really?! That's great!

00:57:04.670 --> 00:57:08.210
Say, was it you who found the bombs, Conan-<i>kun</i>?!

00:57:08.750 --> 00:57:11.880
No, it was Shinichi-<i>niichan</i> who found them!

00:57:12.010 --> 00:57:15.510
Though the bombs haven't actually been found yet...

00:57:19.470 --> 00:57:22.560
The bombs are placed where there wouldn't be shade

00:57:22.640 --> 00:57:25.400
from buildings or walls after 4:00 pm!

00:57:25.600 --> 00:57:28.480
When searching, always be aware of the sun's location

00:57:28.690 --> 00:57:32.900
and be very careful not to cover the bombs with your own shadows!

00:57:45.790 --> 00:57:47.210
Bomb located!

00:57:50.710 --> 00:57:52.050
Bomb located!

00:57:56.050 --> 00:57:57.090
Bomb located!

00:57:58.970 --> 00:58:00.060
Bomb located!

00:58:01.970 --> 00:58:03.350
Bomb located!

00:58:03.520 --> 00:58:04.770
Understood!

00:58:06.600 --> 00:58:09.320
The five bombs have been safely collected.

00:58:09.320 --> 00:58:10.820
- Yes!
- Alright!

00:58:10.900 --> 00:58:13.690
It was all as Kudo-<i>kun</i> deduced...

00:58:14.070 --> 00:58:16.410
Fifteen minutes until sunset...

00:58:16.780 --> 00:58:18.700
Talk about a close call...

00:58:21.040 --> 00:58:23.790
But it's too early to celebrate...

00:58:24.910 --> 00:58:28.670
The amount of explosives used so far accounts for only one-fourth

00:58:28.750 --> 00:58:31.090
of the stolen quantity...

00:58:31.340 --> 00:58:36.340
Meaning that the bomber still has the remaining three-fourths?!

00:58:38.930 --> 00:58:40.140
Sorry I'm late.

00:58:40.220 --> 00:58:41.930
So, what'd you find out?

00:58:42.100 --> 00:58:45.890
Well, about Mayor Okamoto's son Kohei...

00:58:46.560 --> 00:58:50.520
I learned that he left early this morning for the Izu area.

00:58:50.940 --> 00:58:53.030
Which means he's innocent...

00:58:53.190 --> 00:58:54.150
Yes...

00:58:54.360 --> 00:58:56.900
Umm, about the bombing incident...

00:58:56.990 --> 00:58:58.490
Solved.

00:58:58.860 --> 00:59:00.700
All thanks to Kudo-<i>kun...</i>

00:59:00.820 --> 00:59:04.250
The issue now is the remaining explosives and the bomber's identity.

00:59:04.370 --> 00:59:08.750
About all we know for sure is that the bomber doesn't live near

00:59:08.960 --> 00:59:13.340
any of the five spots along the Loop, right?

00:59:15.010 --> 00:59:21.390
Right?! If the bombs blew up, entire trains could've been sent flying!

00:59:21.470 --> 00:59:24.680
He wouldn't risk that near his own house...

00:59:24.810 --> 00:59:31.980
Could that also be why he stopped the timer in the carrying case?!

00:59:32.980 --> 00:59:36.650
There was a playground and an apartment building nearby...

00:59:36.860 --> 00:59:41.030
That's it! The bomber lives in those apartments!

00:59:41.370 --> 00:59:44.830
Alright! Straight to those apartments!

00:59:47.450 --> 00:59:48.790
Nothing at all?!

00:59:48.870 --> 00:59:54.130
Yes. We checked not just that building, but all other nearby houses...

00:59:54.250 --> 00:59:56.010
But they were all in the clear...

00:59:56.840 --> 00:59:58.130
Oh...

00:59:58.260 --> 01:00:03.720
Say, Inspector. What kind of places were the train bombs planted at?

01:00:03.890 --> 01:00:07.930
What kind? Just regular ol' residential areas...

01:00:08.310 --> 01:00:13.020
Oh, yes. There was one on a bridge, over the Sumida Canal.

01:00:13.310 --> 01:00:14.520
On a bridge?

01:00:17.110 --> 01:00:18.570
Isn't this that bridge?

01:00:23.950 --> 01:00:25.160
<i>Hold on...</i>

01:00:25.240 --> 01:00:28.160
<i>Wasn't there a photo of this</i> <i>in Professor Moriya's gallery?</i>

01:00:30.910 --> 01:00:34.840
Say, didn't Professor Moriya design this bridge?

01:00:35.960 --> 01:00:37.420
He did?

01:00:37.420 --> 01:00:38.460
That's correct.

01:00:39.920 --> 01:00:42.260
Moriya Teiji designed it.

01:00:42.640 --> 01:00:46.100
The bridge was completed in 1983,

01:00:46.310 --> 01:00:49.640
and the fact it was built of stone in an English style instead of iron

01:00:49.640 --> 01:00:51.520
was quite the topic at the time.

01:00:51.730 --> 01:00:53.850
With this bridge's design,
Moriya Teiji won

01:00:53.980 --> 01:00:56.770
the Architectural Association of Japan's Newcomer Award!

01:00:56.940 --> 01:00:59.690
You certainly are well-informed!

01:01:00.070 --> 01:01:02.700
Architecture interests me...

01:01:05.620 --> 01:01:09.040
...the recent series of arson incidents. Police believe...

01:01:09.700 --> 01:01:11.410
That's enough.
It's distracting.

01:01:11.500 --> 01:01:12.500
'Kay...

01:01:13.330 --> 01:01:17.340
<i>Come to think of it, the Kurokawa</i> <i>mansion that was set on fire</i>

01:01:17.420 --> 01:01:19.250
<i>was also designed by Professor Moriya...</i>

01:01:22.300 --> 01:01:27.720
Say, I wonder who designed all these houses that were set on fire!

01:01:29.060 --> 01:01:32.850
I bet we might find something interesting if we look into it!

01:01:33.600 --> 01:01:35.310
Interesting, indeed...

01:01:44.320 --> 01:01:45.530
I'll go now.

01:01:45.530 --> 01:01:48.280
Okay. Thanks for coming with me today!

01:01:48.370 --> 01:01:50.580
Better give me the details later!

01:01:50.660 --> 01:01:53.000
Steal at least a kiss from him!

01:02:05.880 --> 01:02:07.140
9:00...

01:02:08.970 --> 01:02:10.430
In one hour...

01:02:08.970 --> 01:02:12.770
"Legend of the Red Thread"

01:02:12.770 --> 01:02:16.020
Say what?! They were all designed by Mr. Moriya?!

01:02:16.100 --> 01:02:16.980
Yes.

01:02:17.060 --> 01:02:21.070
The Kurokawa, Mizushima,
Yasuda, and Akutsu mansions...

01:02:21.190 --> 01:02:23.940
which were all burned down...

01:02:23.940 --> 01:02:26.780
were designed by Professor
Moriya in his early 30s.

01:02:28.780 --> 01:02:31.290
Hard to think it's a coincidence...

01:02:31.290 --> 01:02:36.790
Maybe the bombs on the Loop were really meant for that bridge, too!

01:02:37.420 --> 01:02:38.920
That bridge?!

01:02:38.920 --> 01:02:39.960
It's quite possible.

01:02:39.960 --> 01:02:42.800
The bomber could be the arsonist,

01:02:42.880 --> 01:02:45.420
who's going after
Professor Moriya's designs!

01:02:45.590 --> 01:02:48.760
Aha! That's it, Inspector!

01:02:48.930 --> 01:02:52.060
The culprit is someone with a grudge against Professor Moriya,

01:02:52.140 --> 01:02:54.430
or someone who's jealous of his success!

01:02:54.520 --> 01:02:58.150
His challenge to Shinichi was just camouflage!

01:02:58.480 --> 01:03:01.020
I see. It is highly likely...

01:03:01.020 --> 01:03:02.650
I agree.

01:03:02.780 --> 01:03:07.150
Homemade igniters were used during each arson!

01:03:07.240 --> 01:03:10.990
I now realize they have something in common with the bombings!

01:03:11.870 --> 01:03:15.540
<i>Everything being targeted</i> <i>is work from his 30s...</i>

01:03:15.700 --> 01:03:19.000
Alright! For now, let's go speak with Professor Moriya!

01:03:19.170 --> 01:03:21.130
Mori-<i>kun</i>! Lead the way!

01:03:21.210 --> 01:03:22.710
Right, where was it again?

01:03:22.710 --> 01:03:24.670
I remember, mister!

01:03:25.170 --> 01:03:26.550
I'll lead the way!

01:03:26.760 --> 01:03:28.630
Don't be silly!
You're still not...

01:03:28.630 --> 01:03:30.840
I'm all better now! Come on!

01:03:30.930 --> 01:03:32.140
Hey, wait!

01:03:34.310 --> 01:03:36.230
<i>I leave it to you, Shinichi...</i>

01:03:39.940 --> 01:03:45.110
Mori-<i>san</i>. Just ahead is where the bomb timer temporarily stopped...

01:03:50.450 --> 01:03:52.450
<i>A playground...</i>

01:03:52.830 --> 01:03:57.960
Yeesh! We wasted so much time, all because of those crude bombs!

01:04:14.720 --> 01:04:18.600
I see. That's indeed too much to be a mere coincidence...

01:04:18.600 --> 01:04:22.520
Can you think of anyone who might do something like this?

01:04:22.810 --> 01:04:25.770
Hmm, let me think...

01:04:27.320 --> 01:04:30.740
That's a photograph from when I was ten, Conan-<i>kun.</i>

01:04:31.660 --> 01:04:34.240
With me are my mother and father.

01:04:35.240 --> 01:04:39.290
Your father must be a really great person, Professor Moriya!

01:04:39.910 --> 01:04:43.000
He was a world-renowned architect.

01:04:43.000 --> 01:04:45.500
He was particularly active in England...

01:04:45.590 --> 01:04:48.710
I was a big fan of his architecture...

01:04:49.550 --> 01:04:51.380
I believe he passed away...

01:04:51.680 --> 01:04:54.930
...fifteen years ago, in a fire at his villa.

01:04:55.140 --> 01:04:56.850
Together with my mother...

01:04:57.010 --> 01:05:00.430
I inherited this mansion after it happened.

01:05:01.390 --> 01:05:07.400
And that's when your designs suddenly began to get the spotlight, right, Moriya-<i>san</i>?

01:05:07.610 --> 01:05:10.070
Yes, that's right...

01:05:10.360 --> 01:05:12.910
<i>Huh?! This smell...</i>

01:05:13.570 --> 01:05:14.820
<i>Could it be?!</i>

01:05:15.530 --> 01:05:19.330
Moriya-<i>san</i>. Do you have any ideas who could be behind this?

01:05:19.410 --> 01:05:21.750
Oh, right...

01:05:36.090 --> 01:05:39.720
<i>This is where his works</i> <i>from his 30s begin!</i>

01:05:39.850 --> 01:05:41.100
<i>The Kurokawa mansion...</i>

01:05:41.180 --> 01:05:42.350
<i>The Mizushima mansion...</i>

01:05:42.520 --> 01:05:44.440
<i>The Yasuda mansion</i> <i>and the Akutsu mansion...</i>

01:05:44.520 --> 01:05:45.940
<i>And then the bridge...</i>

01:05:47.360 --> 01:05:49.230
<i>Wait a minute!</i>
<i>This bridge...</i>

01:05:51.360 --> 01:05:52.570
<i>No doubt about it!</i>

01:05:53.150 --> 01:05:57.660
I was still inept in my youth.
Please don't pay them much attention...

01:05:58.530 --> 01:06:01.500
<i>No way! Is that even plausible?!</i>

01:06:01.580 --> 01:06:03.710
<i>But that smell...</i>

01:06:06.120 --> 01:06:08.170
Was this here last time?

01:06:08.920 --> 01:06:12.170
"My Visionary New Town,
West Tama City"?

01:06:12.840 --> 01:06:14.380
Come to think of it...

01:06:14.630 --> 01:06:17.590
As a result of that incident,
Mayor Okamoto lost his position,

01:06:17.680 --> 01:06:25.190
and his plans for a revitalized
West Tama City were scrapped.

01:06:25.730 --> 01:06:29.940
I get it! It was Professor
Moriya who was planning this!

01:06:45.620 --> 01:06:48.380
A new town, with perfect symmetry...

01:06:52.880 --> 01:06:55.300
It's the same as the lampposts in the playground!

01:06:55.970 --> 01:06:58.510
Ah! So that's why...

01:06:59.140 --> 01:07:01.260
That person is the culprit, after all!

01:07:01.350 --> 01:07:03.140
But there's no proof.

01:07:03.220 --> 01:07:07.100
Guess I'll just have to wing it...

01:07:16.030 --> 01:07:17.610
Perfect!

01:07:17.740 --> 01:07:20.200
Now for some scissors, tape, and a marker...

01:07:23.620 --> 01:07:24.620
A lighter?

01:07:25.700 --> 01:07:28.540
I see. So you can't think of anyone...

01:07:28.540 --> 01:07:31.130
I apologize for not being of use.

01:07:31.250 --> 01:07:35.170
Well, if you can think of anything, please let us know.

01:07:35.340 --> 01:07:37.260
Where's Conan-<i>kun</i>?

01:07:38.880 --> 01:07:40.430
Pardon me...

01:07:42.010 --> 01:07:43.180
This is Megure...

01:07:43.390 --> 01:07:44.810
Oh! Kudo-<i>kun</i>!

01:07:46.850 --> 01:07:50.480
Okay! Got it! I'll gather everyone in the gallery right away!

01:07:50.900 --> 01:07:54.940
Moriya-<i>san</i>. I'm sorry to ask, but could we see your gallery?

01:07:55.320 --> 01:08:00.410
Very well. But would you mind if I stopped by my study first?

01:08:00.740 --> 01:08:02.030
Not at all!

01:08:11.920 --> 01:08:14.340
Sorry for the delay.
Right this way...

01:08:16.170 --> 01:08:18.090
The gallery is on the second floor.

01:08:20.840 --> 01:08:22.090
Right in here...

01:08:34.560 --> 01:08:38.490
Megure here.
Yes, we're in the gallery now.

01:08:38.610 --> 01:08:42.410
Inspector Megure. Press the speaker button so that everyone can hear.

01:08:42.490 --> 01:08:43.450
Alright...

01:08:45.080 --> 01:08:49.660
Actually, I've figured out who's behind these arsons and bombings!

01:08:49.790 --> 01:08:53.380
You have?!
Who is it?!

01:08:53.460 --> 01:08:56.290
Hold it! I've figured it out, too!

01:08:57.750 --> 01:09:00.130
The culprit is you,
Detective Shiratori!

01:09:00.970 --> 01:09:02.220
What?!

01:09:03.340 --> 01:09:06.640
As someone with deep respect for Professor Moriya's father,

01:09:06.640 --> 01:09:10.640
you were suspicious about his death and began to suspect his son,

01:09:10.640 --> 01:09:13.650
who had stepped into the spotlight immediately afterward!

01:09:14.060 --> 01:09:17.770
You were suspicious that he had set the fire that killed him!

01:09:17.940 --> 01:09:23.860
Certain of this, you set fire to each of Professor Moriya's buildings!

01:09:23.990 --> 01:09:28.540
Your respect for the father became desire for revenge against the son!

01:09:29.240 --> 01:09:34.540
What's more, you were always absent whenever the bomber called!

01:09:34.540 --> 01:09:36.880
H-hold on, now!

01:09:37.000 --> 01:09:39.920
Well, Shinichi?! Isn't that what you wanna say, too?!

01:09:40.010 --> 01:09:40.710
No!

01:09:40.800 --> 01:09:41.920
What?!

01:09:43.380 --> 01:09:45.800
These incidents were not perpetrated by someone

01:09:45.800 --> 01:09:48.470
with a grudge against Professor Moriya!

01:09:48.640 --> 01:09:51.810
The one responsible is the designer of the four mansions set on fire,

01:09:52.020 --> 01:09:56.310
as well as the bridge...
You, Professor Moriya!

01:09:58.360 --> 01:10:00.150
What?!

01:10:02.690 --> 01:10:07.530
You idiot! What kind of architect destroys his own work?!

01:10:07.780 --> 01:10:13.080
Early on, Professor Moriya inherited his father's architectural talent,

01:10:13.290 --> 01:10:17.460
and in his early 30s, he made his unusually young debut into the architectural world.

01:10:17.630 --> 01:10:19.170
Hello?

01:10:19.380 --> 01:10:22.170
And with his design of the bridge on the Loop,

01:10:22.300 --> 01:10:25.970
he won the Architectural Association of Japan's Newcomer Award!

01:10:26.840 --> 01:10:31.010
Professor Moriya continued to produce new buildings after that,

01:10:31.100 --> 01:10:35.440
when he suddenly... or maybe not so suddenly...

01:10:35.640 --> 01:10:38.810
wanted to get rid of the works he created in his youth.

01:10:39.310 --> 01:10:44.360
This can be surmised from the professor's words at the tea party...

01:10:45.070 --> 01:10:49.030
Most young architects these days lack artistic sense!

01:10:49.120 --> 01:10:53.410
They need to feel much more responsibility for their works!

01:10:53.540 --> 01:10:56.290
In short, you put those words into action.

01:10:56.620 --> 01:10:58.750
That does sound familiar...

01:10:59.040 --> 01:11:02.000
Hold on! You weren't even at his party! How do you...

01:11:02.000 --> 01:11:03.130
Now then, everyone.

01:11:02.840 --> 01:11:04.050
<i>Hey...</i>

01:11:04.170 --> 01:11:05.970
Have a look at the panel photographs.

01:11:06.550 --> 01:11:10.350
Look closely at the Kurokawa mansion, the Mizushima mansion, the Yasuda mansion,

01:11:10.350 --> 01:11:13.220
and the Akutsu mansion, as well as the bridge.

01:11:13.930 --> 01:11:17.560
They each use classic
English-style architecture,

01:11:17.810 --> 01:11:20.480
but do you notice anything about them?

01:11:20.730 --> 01:11:24.320
They all look like splendid works of architecture to me...

01:11:24.320 --> 01:11:27.320
They're not perfectly symmetrical!

01:11:27.450 --> 01:11:31.280
Correct! Their left-right symmetries are slightly off.

01:11:31.780 --> 01:11:34.410
Most likely, the clients ordered it that way,

01:11:34.490 --> 01:11:38.620
or he had to compromise due to building laws or the like.

01:11:39.790 --> 01:11:44.630
Professor Moriya, being a perfectionist, couldn't stand that.

01:11:45.340 --> 01:11:48.170
Around the same time, a shadow began to creep

01:11:48.170 --> 01:11:51.970
into his life as an architect, which had been smooth-sailing until then.

01:11:52.890 --> 01:11:54.970
His plan for a revitalized
West Tama City,

01:11:55.140 --> 01:11:58.020
which he had spent a great deal of time on...

01:11:58.390 --> 01:12:02.110
...was suddenly cancelled as a result of the mayor's arrest!

01:12:03.480 --> 01:12:06.940
Ah! So Professor Moriya designed this, too?!

01:12:07.240 --> 01:12:11.070
By challenging me and tarnishing my name as a high school detective,

01:12:11.070 --> 01:12:13.490
the professor hoped to exact revenge on me,

01:12:13.490 --> 01:12:18.710
while also trying to camouflage his goal, the bridge's destruction...

01:12:18.790 --> 01:12:22.170
to look unrelated to the recent string of mansion arsons!

01:12:23.540 --> 01:12:27.300
And the reason he stopped the bomb timer in the carrying case...

01:12:28.050 --> 01:12:30.930
...was because of the gas lampposts in the playground!

01:12:31.680 --> 01:12:35.680
They were a symbol of his new West Tama City!

01:12:36.930 --> 01:12:39.310
The professor didn't want to destroy them;

01:12:39.430 --> 01:12:44.360
he designed them to resemble the ones from his beloved London!

01:12:44.980 --> 01:12:45.980
Am I wrong?!

01:12:48.150 --> 01:12:50.360
An interesting theory, Kudo-<i>kun...</i>

01:12:50.740 --> 01:12:54.740
But unfortunately, there is no proof.

01:12:54.820 --> 01:12:57.870
Oh, but there is...
Behind the model case!

01:13:01.370 --> 01:13:03.790
This is the bomber's disguise!

01:13:03.790 --> 01:13:06.040
Impossible!
That's in my safe in the study!

01:13:06.040 --> 01:13:11.800
Oh, so the bomber's disguise is actually hidden in your safe?

01:13:12.090 --> 01:13:13.090
What?!

01:13:15.100 --> 01:13:17.220
These are my glasses!

01:13:18.260 --> 01:13:20.480
I painted them black with a marker!

01:13:22.850 --> 01:13:26.650
I made the mustache and wig by cutting that helmet's decorative hair

01:13:26.650 --> 01:13:28.150
and then taping it together!

01:13:28.650 --> 01:13:31.530
These were all Shinichi-<i>niichan</i>'s ideas!

01:13:33.030 --> 01:13:35.530
Professor Moriya. I must ask you to come down to the...

01:13:36.280 --> 01:13:37.370
Don't move!

01:13:37.450 --> 01:13:40.620
Move, and I'll blow the bombs
I set in this mansion!

01:13:41.750 --> 01:13:43.160
They won't blow up.

01:13:43.750 --> 01:13:45.580
After all, that detonator...

01:13:46.040 --> 01:13:47.340
...has no batteries!

01:13:47.420 --> 01:13:48.880
Impossible!

01:13:50.420 --> 01:13:52.050
W-when did you...

01:13:52.050 --> 01:13:54.800
How did you know this was a detonator?!

01:13:54.930 --> 01:13:57.600
Well, you don't use lighters!

01:13:57.720 --> 01:14:00.470
Plus you used long matches to light your pipe...

01:14:01.770 --> 01:14:06.520
...and the sweet smell Ayumi-<i>chan</i> mentioned was your pipe's smell!

01:14:06.810 --> 01:14:08.610
Arrest him!

01:14:11.690 --> 01:14:14.990
Alright! That solves all the cases!

01:14:15.070 --> 01:14:16.780
What a happy ending!

01:14:16.870 --> 01:14:22.660
It's hardly happy, Mori-<i>san</i>!
You're horrible, calling people criminals!

01:14:22.750 --> 01:14:27.460
Yeah, sorry about that! Even monkeys fall from trees, as they say!

01:14:28.630 --> 01:14:32.800
<i>Though in his case,</i> <i>his theories fell instead...</i>

01:14:35.050 --> 01:14:38.640
You're gravely mistaken if you think you've resolved everything.

01:14:38.970 --> 01:14:42.520
There is one other building
I wanted to get rid of!

01:14:45.850 --> 01:14:47.940
No! The Beika City Building?!

01:14:49.310 --> 01:14:52.230
Don't tell me it doesn't have perfect symmetry too?!

01:14:52.320 --> 01:14:55.110
All because of the absurd reason that the building budget was lost

01:14:55.110 --> 01:14:57.740
due to the bubble economy's collapse!

01:14:57.820 --> 01:15:00.950
It's my grandest and lousiest work of all!

01:15:00.950 --> 01:15:03.910
None of you would ever understand my aesthetics!

01:15:04.040 --> 01:15:07.290
Well, then.
One minute to 10:00...

01:15:07.920 --> 01:15:08.960
<i>Ran...</i>

01:15:11.090 --> 01:15:15.010
"Beika City Building -

01:15:11.090 --> 01:15:15.010
Beika Cinema 1"

01:15:23.890 --> 01:15:25.310
Yes, this is Mori...

01:15:25.480 --> 01:15:27.850
Ran-<i>neechan</i>!
Get out, quick!

01:15:44.080 --> 01:15:46.160
Ran-<i>neechan</i>! Are you okay?!
Ran-<i>neechan</i>!

01:15:46.160 --> 01:15:47.250
Gimme that!

01:15:47.330 --> 01:15:50.170
Hey, Ran! What happened?!
Respond! Ran!

01:15:50.420 --> 01:15:51.880
Damn it!

01:15:52.210 --> 01:15:55.710
What the hell are you doing to my Ran?!

01:15:56.340 --> 01:16:00.180
I've only blocked the lobby's entrance and emergency exits so far.

01:16:00.300 --> 01:16:02.010
The best is yet to come...

01:16:02.010 --> 01:16:03.140
What?!

01:16:03.260 --> 01:16:06.430
Hey, Kudo! I assume you're listening from somewhere!

01:16:06.520 --> 01:16:11.020
You better hurry before your beloved girlfriend winds up in scraps!

01:16:11.020 --> 01:16:12.940
You'll pay for this!

01:16:12.940 --> 01:16:14.190
Mori-<i>kun</i>!
No violence!

01:16:17.530 --> 01:16:19.030
What're you doing, kid?!

01:16:21.320 --> 01:16:22.490
These are...

01:16:22.820 --> 01:16:25.240
What the - Bomb blueprints?!

01:16:25.240 --> 01:16:26.120
What?!

01:16:25.870 --> 01:16:27.830
I'll go give them to Shinichi-<i>niichan</i>!

01:16:27.830 --> 01:16:29.370
Hold on!

01:16:29.370 --> 01:16:32.040
I'll send the bomb disposal unit right away!

01:16:38.210 --> 01:16:41.090
<i>I can't wait for the bomb disposal unit!</i>

01:16:42.340 --> 01:16:43.510
Wait!

01:16:44.180 --> 01:16:46.350
If you see Kudo, tell him this!

01:16:46.470 --> 01:16:51.100
"I gave you three minutes!
Enjoy it all you can!"

01:16:53.190 --> 01:16:54.650
Wait, Conan-<i>kun</i>!

01:16:54.650 --> 01:16:56.940
Shiratori-<i>kun</i>!
Take care of Professor Moriya!

01:16:57.070 --> 01:16:58.030
Right!

01:17:33.020 --> 01:17:34.230
Ran!

01:17:34.310 --> 01:17:36.400
Where are you, Ran?!

01:17:36.610 --> 01:17:38.940
Ran! Ran! Damn it!

01:17:38.610 --> 01:17:39.530
<i>Mori-kun</i>!

01:17:39.530 --> 01:17:41.150
Ran!

01:17:41.240 --> 01:17:44.740
Inspector! What are the rescue units doing?!

01:17:45.200 --> 01:17:47.780
Calm down, Mori-<i>kun</i>!
Calm down!

01:17:50.910 --> 01:17:53.460
<i>Hold on, Ran!</i>
<i>I'm coming!</i>

01:18:13.600 --> 01:18:16.310
It's all right!
Help will be here soon!

01:18:22.900 --> 01:18:23.740
Hello?

01:18:23.740 --> 01:18:24.740
R-Ran?!

01:18:24.740 --> 01:18:26.410
S-Shinichi?!

01:18:26.410 --> 01:18:29.370
Lucky! Looks like the phone lines haven't been cut yet!

01:18:29.370 --> 01:18:33.450
Where were you?! You're always gone at the most important times!

01:18:33.450 --> 01:18:36.620
You're really always, always...

01:18:36.620 --> 01:18:39.540
Do you even know what situation I'm in now?!

01:18:39.630 --> 01:18:41.460
Yeah, I know.

01:18:41.670 --> 01:18:45.590
I'm right in front of the emergency exit.
It's blocked with debris...

01:18:50.720 --> 01:18:54.680
I managed to squeeze through the rubble to get here...

01:18:55.020 --> 01:18:57.020
...but the shock from the bomb...

01:18:58.600 --> 01:19:03.070
...seems to have deformed the door, so there's no way to open it...

01:19:03.280 --> 01:19:08.490
Say, is there anything weird in the lobby, like a briefcase or suitcase?

01:19:08.570 --> 01:19:09.780
Weird?

01:19:24.840 --> 01:19:28.260
What is this?
It's really heavy and big!

01:19:28.380 --> 01:19:30.760
And there's this digital clock on it...

01:19:31.140 --> 01:19:33.560
Be careful!
That's a bomb!

01:19:33.720 --> 01:19:34.930
A bomb?!

01:19:38.810 --> 01:19:42.610
<i>Damn you, Professor!</i>
<i>You put the biggest one here!</i>

01:19:42.730 --> 01:19:44.320
Ran! What's the timer say?!

01:19:44.440 --> 01:19:45.570
Hold on!

01:19:47.950 --> 01:19:50.280
42 minutes and 7 seconds...

01:19:50.450 --> 01:19:52.070
<i>42 minutes, huh...</i>

01:19:52.490 --> 01:19:54.830
<i>Which means it'll explode</i> <i>three minutes after midnight...</i>

01:19:55.290 --> 01:19:56.200
<i>Three minutes?</i>

01:19:56.910 --> 01:20:00.500
"I gave you three minutes!
Enjoy it all you can!"

01:20:01.290 --> 01:20:03.090
<i>What is this "three minutes" thing?!</i>

01:20:07.260 --> 01:20:08.010
Well?!

01:20:08.090 --> 01:20:10.640
It's no use! All stairwells are buried in debris.

01:20:10.640 --> 01:20:15.640
It'll take more time to reach the people trapped in the 5th floor lobby!

01:20:17.480 --> 01:20:18.390
<i>Ran...</i>

01:20:21.400 --> 01:20:22.860
<i>18 minutes left!</i>

01:20:22.860 --> 01:20:25.190
<i>There's no time left!</i>
<i>We have no choice...</i>

01:20:25.900 --> 01:20:28.780
Hey, Ran! Do you got any scissors on you?

01:20:28.860 --> 01:20:32.950
I have sewing kit scissors, but what are we going to do with those?

01:20:34.740 --> 01:20:38.080
You're going to disarm the bomb!

01:20:39.960 --> 01:20:42.420
Now listen, follow my instructions...

01:20:42.750 --> 01:20:46.000
Wait! I can't do it while on the phone!

01:20:46.000 --> 01:20:47.260
I'll go by you!

01:20:47.460 --> 01:20:48.460
Wait!

01:20:50.090 --> 01:20:53.300
Alright. There doesn't seem to be a vibration detector on it...

01:20:53.510 --> 01:20:54.930
But do it gently!

01:20:54.930 --> 01:20:55.970
Alright!

01:21:07.280 --> 01:21:08.690
Can you hear me, Shinichi?

01:21:08.690 --> 01:21:10.820
Yeah, loud and clear!

01:21:13.530 --> 01:21:15.120
I'm tearing the bag now.

01:21:15.120 --> 01:21:16.200
Be careful!

01:21:25.840 --> 01:21:27.750
What is it Ran?
Are you all right?

01:21:27.880 --> 01:21:30.300
Y-yeah... I'm fine...

01:21:40.810 --> 01:21:43.310
Okay! I'm ready!

01:21:43.520 --> 01:21:48.570
Alright. First, let's remove the outer cover. Pull it up and off.

01:21:48.860 --> 01:21:49.940
Gently, now!

01:21:49.940 --> 01:21:51.150
R-right...

01:21:55.240 --> 01:21:56.740
It's off, Shinichi!

01:21:56.740 --> 01:22:00.450
Great! Now we're going to cut the wiring inside...

01:22:01.540 --> 01:22:04.170
Mess up the order in the slightest and we're goners!

01:22:07.080 --> 01:22:10.380
First, the yellow cord near the bottom...

01:22:17.350 --> 01:22:18.350
I'm cutting it!

01:22:18.430 --> 01:22:19.470
Okay!

01:22:27.150 --> 01:22:29.440
Inspector! Don't tell me Ran is...

01:22:29.440 --> 01:22:33.440
Calm down, Mori-<i>kun</i>!
That isn't where Ran-<i>kun</i> is!

01:22:33.530 --> 01:22:38.370
Don't worry! Your daughter still has 15 minutes until she's blown up!

01:22:38.530 --> 01:22:43.910
Damn you! Talk!
How do we stop the bomb?!

01:22:43.910 --> 01:22:46.170
It's a special bomb, you see...

01:22:46.370 --> 01:22:52.090
Even if it can be disarmed, the last wire will determine her fate!

01:22:54.590 --> 01:22:58.680
Several pillars of smoke are rising from the Beika City Building...

01:23:05.270 --> 01:23:06.770
It's cut.

01:23:08.480 --> 01:23:11.440
Alright... It looks like we'll make it in time!

01:23:11.520 --> 01:23:14.650
Once we cut the final black cord, the timer'll stop!

01:23:14.820 --> 01:23:16.200
The black cord?

01:23:21.030 --> 01:23:22.700
S-Shinichi...

01:23:22.910 --> 01:23:26.160
I cut the black cord, but the timer isn't stopping...

01:23:26.830 --> 01:23:30.250
P-plus there are still two cords left!

01:23:30.250 --> 01:23:31.670
A red one and a blue one!

01:23:31.670 --> 01:23:33.130
What?!

01:23:36.380 --> 01:23:40.220
The path to the 4th floor stairway is finally open!

01:23:40.390 --> 01:23:44.680
Hurry! There's only four minutes until it detonates!

01:23:44.680 --> 01:23:46.520
Ran! Ran!
I'm coming!

01:23:46.600 --> 01:23:47.640
Mori-<i>san</i>!

01:23:47.640 --> 01:23:49.730
Where are you going, Mori-<i>san</i>?!

01:23:49.810 --> 01:23:53.020
Let go of me!
I have to save Ran!

01:23:53.020 --> 01:23:56.740
Please stop!
The rescue team will save...

01:23:55.650 --> 01:23:57.990
Ran! Ran!

01:23:58.900 --> 01:24:01.950
The hapless love of a father for his daughter...

01:24:02.160 --> 01:24:04.450
Architecture has no need for love...

01:24:04.580 --> 01:24:06.000
Nor does life!

01:24:07.710 --> 01:24:11.330
<i>Wait, Professor! Don't tell me</i> <i>you purposely left out the two wires</i>

01:24:11.330 --> 01:24:13.500
<i>to set me up?!</i>

01:24:13.840 --> 01:24:16.260
What should I do?
Cut them both?

01:24:16.510 --> 01:24:18.970
You idiot!
One of them's a booby trap!

01:24:19.090 --> 01:24:20.720
It'll blow the instant you cut it!

01:24:20.720 --> 01:24:22.550
A-are you serious?!

01:24:30.100 --> 01:24:32.190
<i>Damn! Which is it?!</i>

01:24:32.350 --> 01:24:35.360
<i>Red or blue?!</i>
<i>Which should we cut?!</i>

01:24:50.960 --> 01:24:53.750
Midnight...
Three minutes left...

01:24:54.040 --> 01:24:57.250
Damn it! Which is it?!
Which one?!

01:24:57.250 --> 01:24:58.460
Shinichi?

01:24:58.670 --> 01:24:59.720
Yeah?

01:25:00.720 --> 01:25:03.340
Happy birthday, Shinichi...

01:25:05.140 --> 01:25:06.220
After all...

01:25:07.180 --> 01:25:11.980
I... might never get to say it again...

01:25:12.940 --> 01:25:13.900
<i>Ran...</i>

01:25:24.490 --> 01:25:39.760
<i>Arm in arm, a merry couple strolled by,</i> <i>their voices just bursting out</i>

01:25:30.450 --> 01:25:31.710
Cut it...

01:25:32.830 --> 01:25:34.580
Cut whichever color you want...

01:25:34.790 --> 01:25:37.290
But... what if I get it wrong?

01:25:38.090 --> 01:25:39.840
It doesn't matter.

01:25:39.920 --> 01:25:42.380
We're goners anyway, once time is up...

01:25:40.380 --> 01:25:54.390
<i>I grew a little jealous</i> <i>as I was reminded that you weren't here</i>

01:25:42.550 --> 01:25:45.340
So choose your color...

01:25:45.470 --> 01:25:47.140
B-but...

01:25:50.270 --> 01:25:56.360
Don't worry! I'll be right here with you until you're done cutting!

01:25:56.480 --> 01:26:10.120
<i>You know, when my heart</i> <i>lets its guard down, it wants to be weak</i>

01:25:58.270 --> 01:26:00.150
We'll be together when we die...

01:26:03.320 --> 01:26:04.450
<i>Shinichi...</i>

01:26:10.370 --> 01:26:26.970
<i>so, yes, I gritted my teeth</i> <i>and tried putting on a forced smile</i>

01:26:27.180 --> 01:26:33.350
<i>I want to see you, right now</i>

01:26:30.310 --> 01:26:32.980
Which color do you like better, red or blue?

01:26:33.350 --> 01:26:34.890
Red, I guess?

01:26:35.060 --> 01:26:39.770
<i>I want to see you</i>

01:26:35.060 --> 01:26:39.770
And look! Both Shinichi and I have red as our lucky color for May!

01:26:39.860 --> 01:26:42.990
So I decided that we gotta see this!

01:26:53.790 --> 01:26:56.080
Ran! Ran! You alright?!

01:26:56.670 --> 01:26:58.460
Damn! She can't hear me!

01:26:58.580 --> 01:27:00.210
Oh, yeah!
My cell phone!

01:27:00.380 --> 01:27:01.300
It's gone!

01:27:01.550 --> 01:27:03.420
Damn, did I drop it earlier?!

01:27:03.590 --> 01:27:05.760
T-there's a little boy here!

01:27:07.470 --> 01:27:10.300
You're safe now, little boy! Let's go!

01:27:10.390 --> 01:27:14.850
W-wait! There are still people trapped inside!

01:27:14.850 --> 01:27:16.600
Alright, wait here!

01:27:19.770 --> 01:27:21.730
It's no use!
Get the jackhammer!

01:27:21.730 --> 01:27:22.570
Right!

01:27:23.610 --> 01:27:25.650
Today's my wedding anniversary,

01:27:25.650 --> 01:27:28.200
but it doesn't look like
I'll be enjoying it much...

01:27:29.870 --> 01:27:33.580
"I gave you three minutes!
Enjoy it all you can!"

01:27:34.290 --> 01:27:40.000
<i>I get it! He was telling me</i> <i>to enjoy three minutes of my birthday!</i>

01:27:41.210 --> 01:27:43.170
<i>Wait! Wasn't that when...</i>

01:27:43.670 --> 01:27:46.590
Oh, that sounds like fun!

01:27:46.800 --> 01:27:49.470
I take it you've already gotten him a present?

01:27:49.550 --> 01:27:51.680
No, on Saturday
I'm going to...

01:27:51.800 --> 01:27:55.270
He and I both like the color red!

01:27:55.600 --> 01:27:58.520
And we both have red as our lucky color for May!

01:27:58.810 --> 01:28:00.270
<i>Lucky color?</i>

01:28:00.650 --> 01:28:02.060
<i>Oh no!</i>

01:28:03.770 --> 01:28:05.860
Run, little boy!

01:28:06.320 --> 01:28:07.610
Little boy!

01:28:06.650 --> 01:28:08.700
Ran! The red one's a trap!

01:28:08.700 --> 01:28:10.740
Cut the blue one!
Don't cut the red one!

01:28:10.740 --> 01:28:12.910
Ran, where are you?! Respond!

01:28:21.960 --> 01:28:24.710
Ran! Ran! Ran!

01:28:24.880 --> 01:28:26.460
Ran!

01:28:44.900 --> 01:28:47.530
<i>Goodbye, Shinichi...</i>

01:28:47.940 --> 01:28:48.900
Ran!

01:29:23.900 --> 01:29:25.980
I-impossible!

01:29:45.750 --> 01:29:50.260
It's so wonderful that Ran-<i>kun</i> is all right, Mori-<i>kun</i>!

01:29:50.340 --> 01:29:52.510
Yes! Thank you!

01:29:52.510 --> 01:29:54.220
- I'm with Nichiuri TV!
- Give us your thoughts!

01:29:54.220 --> 01:29:56.300
What role did the great detective play?!

01:29:56.300 --> 01:30:02.520
These bombings were meant to tarnish my name as a great detective

01:30:02.600 --> 01:30:05.850
by leading my daughter Ran into a trap that...

01:30:08.770 --> 01:30:09.610
Oh!

01:30:13.400 --> 01:30:17.200
Conan-<i>kun</i>! You came because you were worried?

01:30:17.200 --> 01:30:18.660
Yeah...

01:30:18.660 --> 01:30:20.660
Where'd you get that bandage?

01:30:20.870 --> 01:30:22.620
Oh, I just fell...

01:30:22.620 --> 01:30:24.500
You need to be careful.

01:30:24.830 --> 01:30:27.460
Say, Conan-<i>kun.</i>
Have you seen Shinichi?

01:30:27.630 --> 01:30:30.460
Huh? He was just here a minute ago...

01:30:30.590 --> 01:30:33.300
Ugh! After I went and got him a present...

01:30:33.590 --> 01:30:37.050
Come to think of it,
Shinichi-<i>niichan</i> did seem puzzled!

01:30:37.300 --> 01:30:40.640
He thought you'd pick the red wire for sure,

01:30:40.640 --> 01:30:43.390
so he was wondering why you cut the blue one instead...

01:30:44.100 --> 01:30:46.850
I didn't want to cut it.

01:30:48.020 --> 01:30:50.440
"Legend of the Red Thread"

01:30:48.020 --> 01:30:50.440
The legendary love starts from here! What is your true color?

01:30:49.110 --> 01:30:52.030
After all, Shinichi and I...

01:30:53.490 --> 01:30:55.650
...might be connected!

01:31:26.230 --> 01:31:33.780
I truly feel sorry for not being able to say things well

01:31:26.230 --> 01:31:33.780
umaku hanashi ga dekinakute hontou wa sumanai to omotteru

01:31:34.070 --> 01:31:41.380
I mulled it over a while, but I eventually fell asleep from exhaustion

01:31:34.070 --> 01:31:41.380
shibaraku nayan demo mita kedo sono uchi tsukarete nemutteru

01:31:41.660 --> 01:31:49.300
On the weekends, this town's air is stuffy and makes me choke,

01:31:41.660 --> 01:31:49.300
shuumatsu no kono machi no kuuki wa hito ikire de muse kaeri

01:31:49.580 --> 01:31:57.180
and when I sighed deeply, it was blotted out by the outdoor speakers

01:31:49.580 --> 01:31:57.180
fukaku tameiki wo tsuitara gaitou supiikaa ni kesareta

01:31:58.430 --> 01:32:12.110
Even when I put the words together, they're never meant to be said

01:31:58.430 --> 01:32:12.110
sorerashii kotoba wo narabete mo tsutawaru koto nado hajime kara nai

01:32:12.650 --> 01:32:27.550
The voice I shout as loudly as I can into the sky over this bustling city

01:32:12.650 --> 01:32:27.550
nigiyaka na kono machi no sora ni omoikiri hariageta koe wa

01:32:27.830 --> 01:32:36.810
is my "Happy Birthday" to that person, in some other faraway city

01:32:27.830 --> 01:32:36.810
doko ka tooku no machi ni iru ano hito e no Happy Birthday

01:32:53.350 --> 01:33:23.730
The voice I shout as loudly as I can into the sky over this bustling city

01:32:53.350 --> 01:33:23.730
nigiyaka na kono machi no sora ni omoikiri hariageta koe wa

01:33:24.010 --> 01:33:33.990
is my "Happy Birthday" to that person, in some other faraway city

01:33:24.010 --> 01:33:33.990
doko ka tooku no machi ni iru ano hito e no Happy Birthday

01:34:00.210 --> 01:34:02.630
<i>T-there's no red thread!</i>

01:34:03.880 --> 01:34:06.930
<i>Guess that means I'm outta luck</i> <i>as long as I'm Conan...</i>
